    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2574": {
      "title": "Technical Specialist",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Technical Specialist Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Technical Specialist Apply for job Job reference: 552540 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Chemistry and Forensics Closing date: 18/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade G (£33,739 - £38,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse community. Inclusive Research. Rewarding Careers. Doing things differently. Technical Specialist - Chemistry Salary- £33,739 - £38,825 per annum Full Time/ Fixed Term contract ( 9 Months ) About the Role One exciting vacancy has arisen for a Technical Specialist in Chemistry to manage a suite of research labs.. The role involves working with the chemistry academic team to support undergraduate and masters level teaching and research projects, in the areas of Chemistry and physical science The post holder will be responsible for ensuring that the research labs are kept to the highest standards of Health and Safety, cleanliness, and organisation. Equipment within these spaces will be maintained and demonstrated to students during practical sessions. Training on equipment for research students and junior staff members will also be undertaken. Excellent communication skills are essential to liaise with the academic team to determine technical requirements, manage the workload of the technical team, and to assist students in the labs where required. This is an exciting opportunity for an enthusiastic and motivated individual with relevant experience, either within a higher education/training environment, or industry. Ideally the post holder will have previous managerial experience. You will also be expected to be flexible and support colleagues and students in other areas of the School of Science and Technology, as part of a School-wide technical team. Other essential competencies for the job are organisation, leadership, adaptability, and a commitment to a high-quality customer experience. We are committed to delivering outstanding teaching and world-leading research, that changes lives and society. If you are ambitious to shape the future, and contribute to our mission, come and join our exciting team of enthusiastic staff and students. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: w/c 26th October 2026 About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. In the Department of Chemistry, courses are taught in modern, innovative spaces, offering excellent career prospects and accreditation by The Royal Society of Chemistry. The Department has an active research community with a diverse range of knowledge and expertise. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Diego Lo Destro (Technical Team Leader) at diego.lodestro@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2639": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Paramedicine",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer in Paramedicine Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer in Paramedicine Apply for job Job reference: 552604 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care Closing date: 28/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Social Sciences Salary / Grade HE Lecturer (£39,984 - £43,671 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Inspire, drive change and save lives. Doing things differently. Lecturer in Paramedicine Salary- £39,984 - £43,671 per annum Full time/ permanent About the Role The Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care at Nottingham Trent University is looking to appoint an enthusiastic and forward-thinking Paramedic Lecturer to join our academic team. We’re seeking an individual who is experienced in the field of Paramedicine and who can provide high quality teaching and learning for our students. The successful candidate will join the Paramedic Team to make a valued contribution to our range of Paramedic, ambulance practice and continuing professional development courses. You will participate in the planning, delivery, assessment, and quality assurance processes across the Paramedic programmes. You will contribute to student recruitment for both the courses. You will act as a personal tutor for Paramedic students and apprentices, providing pastoral care, and coordinating progress reviews for apprentices, working collaboratively with our key stakeholder organisations to ensure support and high-quality learning experiences for students. The successful candidate will have experience working with learners in practice or higher education, designing, and delivering learning opportunities, and have a good understanding of current and evolving clinical, professional, and policy developments in Paramedicine. You will possess excellent communication skills with a willingness to continue developing your scholarly, practice, or research profile. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: Thursday 5th November 2026 About Us Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care brings together expert and enthusiastic staff from across the health, social care, and social work sectors, many of whom are experienced practitioners and recognised leaders in their fields. Our academics are actively engaged in research and scholarship, with work that is widely published and directly informs our curriculum, ensuring students benefit from a contemporary, evidence-based and professionally relevant learning experience. We are committed to providing a vibrant, inclusive and supportive learning environment where teaching is grounded in research, professional practice and a strong commitment to student success. By fostering collaboration between students, practitioners, researchers and external partners, we prepare graduates to make a meaningful impact within their professions and communities. The Institute is dedicated to developing innovative education and research that addresses the challenges facing health and social care services today. Through our strong partnerships with healthcare, social care and community organisations, we strive to make a positive contribution to improving health, wellbeing and social outcomes for all. Our ambition is to equip the next generation of professionals with the knowledge, skills and values needed to lead change and improve lives in an evolving health and social care landscape. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Carl Webster, Principal Lecturer Paramedicine at Carl.Webster@ntu.ac.uk or Anne Felton, Academic Director at Anne.Felton@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2561": {
      "title": "Information Assistant",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Information Assistant Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Information Assistant Apply for job Job reference: 552527 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Libraries and Learning Resources Closing date: 18/10/2026 School / Directorate: z.Libraries and Learning Resources Salary / Grade Grade D (£26,336 - £27,434 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Creating Welcoming Spaces for Learning, Teaching and Research. Doing things differently. Information Assistant- Clifton Campus Salary- £26,336 - £27,434 per annum (pro rata) This is an Annualised hours contract- 23 hours per week Working pattern: 9am - 2pm Monday & Tuesday 8:45am - 5:15pm Saturday 1:45pm - 7:15pm Sunday During term-time Plus 8 additional summer Saturdays (10am - 2pm) About the Role At the heart of Nottingham Trent University, our libraries inspire and enable independent learning and research. We actively engage with our customers and make a difference. We create an inspiring physical and on-line environment for learning and research. We want to make it easy for people to use our libraries and learning resources. And that's where you come in. We're looking for an Information Assistant to join our friendly and welcoming customer service team. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: Wednesday 11th November 2026 What you'll be doing This role isn't just checking and sorting books. You'll be an essential support to customers of our libraries and learning resources to providing practical help and guidance. You'll be the go to person for face-face, telephone and online enquiries and assistance. Supporting customers to get online or how to use software one minute and then identifying and referring specialist enquiries the next. No two days will be the same as you'll work, on a rota basis, completing a variety of tasks. What you'll bring You'll bring your excellent customer service skills and ability to work effectively with a wide range of people. If you've got confidence in using IT systems and experience of supporting customers in a busy service environment, then we'd love to hear from you. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. For any informal queries about the role or the LLR team, please contact Grace Carter (User Experience Team Leader) at grace.carter@ntu.ac.uk What we offer We can offer you a career with a difference, as together we shape futures, change lives and create the university of the future. We'll look after you with ongoing support, good development opportunities and a competitive salary that rewards your contribution. We also offer generous holidays, a pension scheme, great facilities and a wide range of savings, discounts and benefits. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2504": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Senior Lecturer - Visual Effects (teaching) Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Senior Lecturer - Visual Effects (teaching) Apply for job Job reference: 552471 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Design and Digital Arts Closing date: 21/10/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham School of Art & Design Salary / Grade HE Senior Lecturer (£46,320 - £58,624 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Senior Lecturer - Visual Effects (Teaching only) (£46,320 - £58,624 p.a. pro rata) Permanent/Part time post 22.2 hours per week - 3 days a week The core purpose of a Teaching-Focused Lecturer is to make a significant contribution to student success through the delivery of high-quality teaching and learning activities within the school. As a key member of the course team, you will contribute to the delivery of modules and course content, helping to ensure students receive an engaging, inclusive and supportive learning experience. You will also support a range of departmental activities, including student recruitment events, departmental meetings and the provision of pastoral support to students. Working closely with course leadership teams, you will help organise teaching resources effectively and play an active role in implementing enhancements to curriculum design and maintaining the school’s high academic standards and excellent student experience and outcomes. You will bring strong subject knowledge, excellent written and verbal communication skills, and confidence in using a range of digital technologies to support learning and teaching. You will be comfortable working both independently and collaboratively and will contribute positively to teaching-related activities across the school. Above all, you will be passionate about supporting students to achieve their potential and succeed in their studies. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview date: TBC About Us Nottingham School of Art & Design is one of the world’s leading art and design schools; we have been influencing, inspiring and innovating for over 175 years. Constantly pushing the boundaries of what’s possible, we’re a diverse community of artists, designers, and creatives at the heart of one of the UK’s most innovative cities. Catalysts of change and new thinking, we nurture the best creative and digital talent. We give our students the freedom to take risks and express their creativity and individuality. We carry out bold, original and daring research. We believe in the power of connectivity, collaborating with creative minds around the globe and working with the creative sector to develop highly employable graduates. We bring different disciplines together to inspire our students to think beyond their passion and make a bigger impact, from sustainability to enterprise and social justice. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Jeremy Moorshead (Principle Lecturer Digital Screen Arts) at jeremy.moorshead@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2563": {
      "title": "Research Associate in Law",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Research Associate in Law Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Research Associate in Law Apply for job Job reference: 552529 Location: City Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Masters and Legal Research Closing date: 06/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Law School Salary / Grade Grade F (£29,352 - £33,739 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Research Associate in Law Salary- £29,352 - £33,739 per annum Full time/Fixed for 12 months About the role Are you looking for an opportunity to develop your research experience while contributing to projects that address important legal and social challenges? As a Research Associate in Law, you will work with academic colleagues across Nottingham Law School. Your work will be varied. Depending on the projects to which you are assigned, you may: search for, review and clearly summarise academic literature, legislation, case law and policy materials; contribute to research reports, journal articles and other publications; help design and undertake qualitative research, which may include interviews, focus groups or document analysis; organise, manage and analyse research data in accordance with ethical and data-protection requirements; undertake horizon-scanning to identify emerging legal, policy and research developments; support colleagues in preparing applications for external research funding; assist with research events and engagement activities; and help communicate research findings to academic, professional and public audiences. You will manage your own agreed tasks while working closely with project leads and other members of the research community based in our three research centres: the Centre for Law, Emerging Technologies and Business, the Centre for Rights and Justice, and the Centre for Legal Education. You may also collaborate with external partners and stakeholders from the public, private and third sectors. This role offers you the opportunity to strengthen your research skills, broaden your knowledge across different areas of law and contribute to research with real-world relevance and impact. You will join a supportive and inclusive research environment in which collaboration, professional development and the exchange of ideas are encouraged. The post is offered on a full-time basis, although consideration will also be given to fractional appointments and job-share arrangements For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: 19th & 20th November 2026 About Us Nottingham Law School (NLS) is one of the leading providers of academic and professional legal education in the country, with an established record of delivering innovative and transformational courses. We are one of the largest law schools in the UK, offering a range of undergraduate degrees, academic and practitioner taught postgraduate courses and a strong research degrees programme. In addition, our students can gain practical experience volunteering at NLS Legal, our multi-award-winning-teaching law firm, the only on-campus law firm at a UK Law School. Research is central to the School’s mission, enabling our work to make a positive difference to lives and society locally, nationally and globally. We foster a vibrant, inclusive and sustainable research environment, supported by a strong research infrastructure. Our approach is founded on the mutually enriching relationship between excellent academic research, professional practice and legal education. Our researchers produce innovative, impactful and world-leading work, often engaging with cross-disciplinary developments and some of the most significant challenges facing society. These include the rights, safety and security of vulnerable groups; the accountability of public- and private-sector bodies; and the financial and environmental sustainability of the public, private and third sectors. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Professor Jonathan Doak (Associate Dean for Research) at jonathan.doak@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Hybrid working - we encourage and offer a mixture of office working and working from home. You're empowered to define how you work best for the benefits of your stakeholders. Flexibility - take ownership over how you get your work done. We're open to different working patterns and approaches. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2614": {
      "title": "Observatory Support Officer",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Observatory Support Officer Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Observatory Support Officer Apply for job Job reference: 552579 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Physics and Maths Closing date: 23/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade G (£33,739 - £38,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse Community. Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Observatory Support Officer Special conditions : A rate of £17.48 will be paid per hour in the role as observatory support officer About the Role The Nottingham Trent University onsite observatory is part of the department of Physical Sciences, one of the School of Science and Technology's five departments, with just below 40 academic colleagues. The observatory supports our work with a variety of observational equipment within Astrophysics across a range of areas including teaching (at foundation, bachelors, and masters levels), research, practice, scholarship and community and commercial engagement. We are seeking to appoint hourly paid Observatory Support Officers that will assist in the delivery of high-quality teaching and learning. Duties will include providing technical support and supervision for activities such as observatory related laboratory supervision, observing sessions, planetarium provision, and problem classes. It will also include delivering small scale outreach events, summer schools, and managing the observatory’s social media presence. Scheduling will acknowledge other academic responsibilities expected for (under-) graduate applicant. Having very good communication skills, the successful applicant must demonstrate commitment to supporting Astronomy teaching (related to working with astronomical equipment) to students within our programmes at FdSc, BSc and Master levels, as well as participants of short courses and summer schools. For more details, please take a look at the profile role. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly Application Details: Please remember to submit both a CV as well as a cover letter (or supporting statement) for your application. Interview Date: Interviews will commence in the first week of November. Dr Brown (Observatory coordinator) will be in touch following the submission of your application. Interview Date: w/c 2nd November 2026. About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our Physical Sciences department has a strong track record of gaining high-calibre research finding and delivering international impact in areas as diverse as acoustic monitoring of honeybees, art conservation and wastewater treatment. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Dr Daniel Brown (Observatory coordinator) at daniel.brown02@ntu.ac.uk . Join Us We can offer you a career with a difference, as together we shape futures, change lives and create the university of the future. Doing things differently, we empower our people to shape, create and innovate. Whether they’re pushing the boundaries with award-winning research, transforming society through global collaborations or supporting and helping our students to achieve their potential. Join our friendly and diverse community of 4,000 professionals, academics and researchers, and you’ll enjoy the support and ownership you need to perform at your best. A great place to work, we value, respect and care for all our colleagues, providing flexible and competitive rewards and genuine opportunities for career progression. So, take on an exciting new challenge with an ambitious university where progress never stops. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Safeguarding Statement Nottingham Trent University is committed to safeguarding and promoting the welfare of young people and expects all colleagues to share this commitment. If you are successful, you will be required to undertake an enhanced application and a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check. The post for which you are applying is exempt from Section 4(2) of the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act 1974 requiring any spent convictions to be declared. Any information you provide will be treated in confidence and only used when considering your suitability for the post. Before you apply we recommend you ensure you are able to supply the documentation listed on the DBS website Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- Observatory Support Officer (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2381": {
      "title": "Admissions Associate",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Admissions Associate Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Admissions Associate Apply for job Job reference: 552349 Location: City Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Admissions Closing date: 16/10/2026 School / Directorate: Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment Salary / Grade Grade E (£28,063 - £30,185 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. Admissions Associate Grade E (£28,063 - £30,185 p.a. pro rata) 12 Months - Fixed Term Contract About the Role Join our Admissions team and play a key role in shaping the journey of future students. As an Admissions Associate, you’ll support the processing of both undergraduate and postgraduate applications, delivering a fast, fair and high-quality service that makes a real difference to applicants and colleagues across the University. We’re looking for someone who is detail-focused, proactive, and thrives in a fast-paced environment. If you enjoy working to targets, solving problems, and putting the customer at the centre of everything you do, we want to hear from you. In this role, you’ll be: Processing applications accurately and efficiently, meeting KPIs and service standards Delivering a seamless, supportive experience for applicants from start to finish Contributing to a fair, inclusive and transparent admissions process Supporting key University events, including Open Days, Confirmation, Clearing and Graduation Ensuring full compliance with key regulations, including GDPR and data confidentiality For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. The Admissions team currently operates a hybrid working model, with colleagues typically based three days per week in our Nottingham city centre office and working remotely for the remainder. Please note that this arrangement may vary, and you may be required to attend the office more frequently at times, particularly for meetings, events, Confirmation, Clearing, and team away days. Interviews; w/c 2nd November 2026 About Us Our award-winning Department of Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) is responsible for engaging with key audiences including prospective students to support NTU’s student recruitment targets and driving forward NTU’s reputation and brand. CAMS comprises admissions, applicant engagement, student recruitment events and outreach, international student recruitment, marketing and campaigns, content management, creative services, social media, web and digital, public relations and internal and external communications. If you have a passion for student recruitment, marketing and communications and a drive to make a real difference, CAMS at NTU could be the perfect place for you. In return, CAMS can offer you a culture of positivity, encouragement and mutual support. The senior leadership team are committed to nurturing talent and helping people reach their full potential. But most of all, CAMS believe in change and growth; in daring to do things differently. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Hannah Thornley (Admissions Manager) at Hannah.Thornley@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe & Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2488": {
      "title": "Catering Assistant",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Catering Assistant Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Catering Assistant Apply for job Job reference: 552455 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Events and Hospitality Closing date: 16/10/2026 School / Directorate: z.Campus Operations Salary / Grade Grade OSE (£25,086 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Support our students at every stage of their journey. Doing things differently. Catering Assistant £25,086 per annum Full Time/Permanent 5 days over 7, including evenings, weekends and occasional events as required Are you someone who enjoys working with people and takes pride in delivering great hospitality? As a Catering Assistant at Nottingham Trent University, you'll be part of NTU's catering team, delivering hospitality across meetings, conferences, events, and university functions. We are looking for a professional, enthusiastic and customer-focused Catering assistant to join our busy hospitality team on a full-time contract of 37 hours per week, working 5 days out of 7 on a rota basis. This is an exciting opportunity for an individual who is passionate about delivering exceptional customer service across a variety of hospitality settings, including formal dining, banqueting, events and delivered hospitality services. About the Role As a catering assistant, you will play a key role in creating outstanding experiences for our customers. Working across multiple hospitality venues and events, you will be responsible for delivering high-quality food and beverage service, anticipating customer needs and ensuring the highest standards of presentation and professionalism are maintained at all times. The successful candidate will be comfortable working in a fast-paced environment, supporting colleagues as part of a team or without supervision, leading by example and helping to ensure smooth day-to-day operations. For more details, please take a look at the job description. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Location: This role supports catering operations across Nottingham Trent University's City, Clifton, Brackenhurst, Mansfield, and Confetti campuses, so flexibility to work across different locations is essential. Interview date: W/C 19th October 2026 About Us Nottingham Trent University is a successful and ambitious university that is recognised for its innovation and inclusivity and being bold enough to do things differently. Our Campus Operations team work tirelessly behind the scenes to support our students. Whether you're making sure our students are safe, serving up delicious meals, or ensuring every package reaches its destination, your role matters. Our team's dedication ensures smooth operations, safety, and exceptional experiences. For any informal queries about the role or the Campus Operations team, please contact Gareth Worth at gareth.worth@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Be part of a supportive and dynamic team —help deliver outstanding service and hospitality in a vibrant, on-site environment. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. And a whole lot more… Come and be part of our success. Apply today! Safe & Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system, upcoming immigration rules (4th April 2024) changes may impact on eligibility for sponsorship, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. Visit https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa for more information. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2656": {
      "title": "Network Coordinator",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Network Coordinator Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Network Coordinator Apply for job Job reference: 552621 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Computer Science Closing date: 19/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade G (£33,739 - £38,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. Network Coordinator- EPSRC Green+ Network Salary- £33,739 - £38,825 per annum Full time/ Fixed term contract for 12 months Important Information: This is an in-person post based in Nottingham. It involves collaboration with other EPSRC-funded networks and international partners. The role requires regular travel across the UK and abroad to support workshops, co-creation activities, tutorials, Hackathons and national level events. About GREEN+ GREEN+ is a national network funded by UKRI through EPSRC. It brings together researchers, green-space providers, healthcare professionals, community organisations and technology developers to explore how AI, sensing and low-energy digital technologies can support physical activity, mental wellbeing and social connectedness in green environments. The Network is led by Professor Eiman Kanjo at Nottingham Trent University, with co-lead Professor Kia Nazarpour at the University of Edinburgh. Role overview We are seeking a proactive and service-focused Network Coordinator to provide reliable operational, administrative and project support to the Network Lead and leadership team. The postholder will help deliver agreed priorities and activities, using initiative to complete assigned work, identify issues and propose improvements within the Network’s strategic direction. Key responsibilities Coordinate the Network’s day-to-day administration and operations. Support events, workshops, sandpits, training, meetings and community-engagement activities. Take responsibility for coordinating and delivering agreed activities, with opportunities to lead specific activities under the direction of the Network Lead. Maintain project plans, records, reports, budgets and stakeholder communications. Liaise with researchers, green-space providers, healthcare professionals, community organisations, industry, government and international partners. Support Network calls, feasibility projects, funding bids, partnerships, laboratories and related academic or institutional initiatives. Provide responsive support to the Network Lead, leadership team and wider consortium. Learn new skills and use AI and digital tools to improve project delivery. Undertake other reasonable duties consistent with the role’s purpose and grade as priorities develop. This is a full-time, 12-month fixed-term post, with the possibility of extension subject to continued funding, performance and operational requirements. Regular workplace attendance and occasional UK or international travel may be required. Further information is available at https://greenplus.uk Please refer to the attached job description and person specification for full details. Interview date: TBC About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our Department of Computer Science combines internationally-significant research with an outstanding record for teaching excellence. Our state-of-the-art facilities and career-focused approach to course design provide the right conditions for students to excel in their chosen fields. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Prof. Eiman Kanjo Head of Smart Sensing Lab at eiman.kanjo@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2498": {
      "title": "Senior Technician",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Senior Technician Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Senior Technician Apply for job Job reference: 552465 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Biosciences Closing date: 25/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade F (£29,352 - £33,739 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse community. Inclusive Research. Rewarding Careers. Doing things differently. Senior Technician Salary- £29,352 - £33,739 per annum Full time/Permanent About the Role As a member of the technical team, you will be expected to demonstrate equipment and techniques and provide support and guidance to students in Bioscience teaching and research laboratories. You will create a positive, industry-relevant learning environment and maintain a safe working environment and escalate issues where necessary. Provide technical support and guidance to academic colleagues in laboratories, workshops, and studios. Ensure all staff and students are working within a safe environment and escalate issues where necessary. Identify appropriate personal development opportunities and actively keep up to date with relevant discipline knowledge, trends, and technology, and apply this learning to practices. Connect with relevant internal and external networks and use these contacts to enhance delivery. Be a team player and support others in creating a positive environment. Interview Date: w/c 09/11/2026 About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our courses in the Department of Biosciences are research-led, providing students with cutting-edge knowledge and access to high-specification facilities. It is one of the many reasons why our courses are accredited by the Institute of Biomedical Science, the Royal Society of Biology and the Chartered Institute of Ecology and Environment Management. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Macsen Fryer (Technical Team Leader) at Macsen.Fryer@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
