    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2630": {
      "title": "Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Criminal Law",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Criminal Law Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Criminal Law Apply for job Job reference: 552595 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Vocational and Professional Programmes Closing date: 18/10/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Law School Salary / Grade HE Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (£39,984 - £58,624 pa pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Shape the Legal Minds of Tomorrow. Doing things differently. Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Criminal Law Lecturer salary- £39,984 - £43,671 per annum Senior Lecturer salary- £46,320 - £58,624 per annum Full time/Permanent About the Role We are looking to appoint a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (depending on experience) to teach on our undergraduate and postgraduate (including practitioner) courses. We welcome applications in the area of Criminal Law. You must hold a professional qualification as any of the following: a solicitor or barrister a chartered legal executive (FCILEX) a trade mark attorney or a patent attorney in the jurisdiction of England and Wales If you are in the early stages of an academic career and are considering joining NTU, then our Early Career Academic Development Programme could be just right for you. If you are considering joining NTU as a Senior Lecturer you will benefit from our Senior Lecturer Career Framework , which recognises and rewards you based on your performance, contribution and achievement, and offers the opportunity of faster salary progression compared to the industry average. Interview date: 29th October 2026 About Us Nottingham Law School (NLS) is one of the leading providers of academic and professional legal education in the country, with an established record of delivering innovative and transformational courses. We are one of the largest law schools in the UK, offering a range of undergraduate degrees, academic and practitioner taught postgraduate courses and a strong research degrees programme. Our School has built a reputation for excellence in the provision of legal education and in shaping the careers of solicitors, barristers and legal practitioners at both national and international levels. In addition to our outstanding research expertise, we have long established links with policy makers, professional bodies and leading law firms, including a growing number of significant international associations. We have an extensive record of delivering excellent bespoke training programmes for practitioners and professional bodies, and have strengths in commissioned research, both in the UK and overseas. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Elyse Wakelin at elyse.wakelin02@ntu.ac.uk or Alexandra Kastrinou at alexandra.kastrinou@ntu.ac.uk . Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2611": {
      "title": "HPL Property Management &amp; Development",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for HPL Property Management &amp; Development Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results HPL Property Management & Development Apply for job Job reference: 552576 Location: City Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Property Management and Development Closing date: 31/07/2027 School / Directorate: School of Architecture, Design and the Built Environment Salary / Grade HPL1 (£39,984- £44,977 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Hourly Paid Lecturer – Property Management & Development £Salary per direct teaching hour. Include any details here specific to role e.g. Length of contract if fixed term This includes 2 or more of the following elements: teaching, preparation and marking of the scheduled programme of work. A flat rate of £Salary per direct teaching hour will be paid for completing one of the above elements of the schedule. The number of hours required and the days of the week may vary. About the Role To support the delivery of the undergraduate and/or postgraduate portfolio within Property Management & Development by making a direct contribution to teaching. The role will encompass all of the following, but the balance of duties and responsibilities will be determined in discussion with the post holder’s line manager: Subject Area Real Estate Building Surveying Valuation Property Management Law Economics Property Development Planning Construction For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. About Us We are the School of Architecture, Design and the Built Environment (ADBE) at Nottingham Trent University. We make, create, design and build. We’re planners and problem solvers. We draw lines, and we break boundaries. We are 3,000 students, five departments and one school. In the School of Architecture, Design and the Built Environment, we stand half way between science and philosophy; and between tradition and disruption. We embrace theoretical rigour and insist on providing hands-on experience for all our students. We celebrate design heritage, and we invite innovation. We’re a nationally renowned stage for talent in making and design. We investigate the physicality of tools and tech, glass and grass, and bricks and mortar. We also explore the abstract excitement of ideas and creative philosophies. For any informal queries about the role or the ADBE team, please contact Keith Lown, Head of Property Management & Development at keith.lown@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt 552576 - Hourly Paid Lecturer Property Management and Development JDPS (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2547": {
      "title": "Lead Coach Athletics",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lead Coach Athletics Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lead Coach Athletics Apply for job Job reference: 552513 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: NTU Sport Closing date: 26/10/2026 School / Directorate: z.University Sports Activities Salary / Grade See special conditions Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. NTU Sport are committed to having 70% of students engaged in sport and physical activity by 2025. Join us on our mission. Lead Athletics Coach £20 per hour Zero Hours About the Role Are you passionate about athletics and helping athletes reach their potential? We're looking for a Lead Athletics Coach to lead and shape the coaching programme for Nottingham Trent University Athletics Club. In this role, you'll plan and deliver engaging training sessions for a diverse group of student-athletes, ranging from recreational participants to performance-level competitors. You'll work closely with club committee members, assistant coaches and NTU Sport staff to create a positive, inclusive and ambitious environment where students can thrive both on and off the track. You'll lead the development of training programmes, support athlete progression and help students balance their sporting commitments alongside university life. You'll also play an important role in supporting assistant coaches and volunteers to deliver an outstanding student experience. We're looking for someone with strong coaching experience, excellent communication skills and a passion for developing people. You'll be confident planning and leading sessions, providing constructive feedback and adapting your coaching approach to meet the needs of a wide range of athletes. Training takes place at Harvey Hadden Sports Village on Tuesday and Thursday evenings during term time. The successful candidate will therefore need to be able to travel to and from the venue on a regular basis. Access to a car may be beneficial but is not essential. Whether you're an experienced university coach or looking to take the next step in your coaching career, we'd love to hear from you Interviews Date: w/c 9th November 2026 About Us At NTU, we believe that sport is for everyone. That's why we are passionate about creating a welcoming and inclusive environment where our students, staff and the people of Nottingham feel inspired, supported and part of a community. Our core values are Pride, Unity and Respect, and these three pillars are embedded into everything we do at NTU Sport. From the way we deliver coaching and sports science support, to the way we design our world–class facilities, we are committed to developing a culture of inclusivity and respect. Our determination to provide an outstanding service helped NTU secure 8th place in the British Universities & Colleges Sports (BUCS) championship 2022-23, cementing NTU as a top 10 university for Sport. Our Facilities We have a fantastic range of sports facilities at our City campuses, including industry-standard gym equipment, a 10m climbing wall, a sports hall, dance studios and a sports therapy suite offering physiotherapy and sports massage. Our Clifton campus is home to the Lee Westwood Sports Centre, a fully floodlit all-weather astro-turf pitch, three brand new squash courts, an exercise studio, sports hall, grass pitches and a newly refurbished fitness suite. Our Equestrian Centre at Brackenhurst features both indoor and outdoor arenas and holds a variety of events throughout the year, including unaffiliated and affiliated dressage competitions, and unaffiliated show jumping. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Steven Drake Club Management Coordinator at steven.drake@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us We’ll look after you with ongoing support, good development opportunities and a competitive salary that rewards your contribution. We also offer generous holidays, flexible working options, a pension scheme, great facilities and wide range of savings, discounts and benefits. Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University Start to think about your future differently. Apply here. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- Lead Coach Athletics (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2508": {
      "title": "Network Coordinator",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Network Coordinator Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Network Coordinator Apply for job Job reference: 552475 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Computer Science Closing date: 19/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade G (£33,739 - £38,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. Network Coordinator- EPSRC Tiny UK Network Salary £33,739 - £38,825 per annum Full time/ Fixed term contract for 12 months Important Information: This is an in-person post based in Nottingham. It involves collaboration with other EPSRC-funded networks and international partners. The role requires regular travel across the UK and abroad to support workshops, co-creation activities, tutorials, Hackathons and national level events. About TinyML UK TinyML UK is a new national network funded by UKRI through EPSRC. It connects researchers, industry, engineers, AI specialists and government organisations working on decentralised, energy-efficient machine learning for small and low-power devices. The Network supports collaboration, training, events and real-world impact across health, sustainability and security, while contributing to a UK roadmap for TinyML research and skills. The Network is led by Professor Eiman Kanjo at Nottingham Trent University, with co-leads Professor Geoff Merrett at the University of Southampton and Professor Pantelis Georgiou at Imperial College London. Role overview We are seeking a proactive and service-focused Network Coordinator to provide reliable operational, administrative and project support to the Network Lead and leadership team. The postholder will help deliver agreed priorities and activities, using initiative to complete assigned work, identify issues and propose improvements within the Network’s strategic direction. Key responsibilities Coordinate the Network’s day-to-day administration and operations. Support large and small events, workshops, training, competitions, meetings and outreach activities. The opportunity to lead activities. Maintain project plans, records, reports, budgets and stakeholder communications. Liaise with academic, industry, government and international partners. Support funding bids, partnerships, laboratories and related academic or institutional initiatives. Provide responsive support to the Network Lead, leadership team and wider consortium. Learn new skills and use AI and digital tools to improve project delivery. Undertake other reasonable duties consistent with the role’s purpose and grade as priorities develop. This is a full-time, 12-month fixed-term post, with the possibility of extension subject to continued funding, performance and operational requirements. Regular workplace attendance and occasional UK or international travel may be required. Further information is available at : https://tinyML.uk Please refer to the attached job description and person specification for full details. Interview date: TBC About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our Department of Computer Science combines internationally-significant research with an outstanding record for teaching excellence. Our state-of-the-art facilities and career-focused approach to course design provide the right conditions for students to excel in their chosen fields. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Prof. Eiman Kanjo Head of Smart Sensing Lab at eiman.kanjo@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2570": {
      "title": "Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Law",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Law Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Law Apply for job Job reference: 552536 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Vocational and Professional Programmes Closing date: 18/10/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Law School Salary / Grade HE Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (£39,984 - £58,624 pa pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Shape the Legal Minds of Tomorrow. Doing things differently. Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Law Salary- Lecturer £39,984-£43,671 per annum Salary- Senior Lecturer £46,320-£58,624 per annum Full time/Permanent About the Role We welcome applications from across all areas of Law, with particular interest in candidates specialising in Criminal Law and Land/ Property Law. You must have recent teaching experience in Higher Education, as well as submitted your PhD or hold a professional qualification as any of the following: a solicitor or barrister a chartered legal executive (FCILEX) a trade mark attorney or a patent attorney in the jurisdiction of England and Wales If you are in the early stages of an academic career and are considering joining NTU, then our Early Career Academic Development Programme could be just right for you. If you are considering joining NTU as a Senior Lecturer you will benefit from our Senior Lecturer Career Framework , which recognises and rewards you based on your performance, contribution and achievement, and offers the opportunity of faster salary progression compared to the industry average. Interview date: 29th October 2026 About Us Nottingham Law School (NLS) is one of the leading providers of academic and professional legal education in the country, with an established record of delivering innovative and transformational courses. We are one of the largest law schools in the UK, offering a range of undergraduate degrees, academic and practitioner taught postgraduate courses and a strong research degrees programme. In addition, our students can gain practical experience volunteering at NLS Legal, our multi-award-winning-teaching law firm, the only on-campus law firm at a UK Law School. Our School has built a reputation for excellence in the provision of legal education and in shaping the careers of solicitors, barristers and legal practitioners at both national and international levels. In addition to our outstanding research expertise, we have long established links with policy makers, professional bodies and leading law firms, including a growing number of significant international associations. We have an extensive record of delivering excellent bespoke training programmes for practitioners and professional bodies, and have strengths in commissioned research, both in the UK and overseas. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Elyse Wakelin at elyse.wakelin02@ntu.ac.uk or Alexandra Kastrinou at alexandra.kastrinou@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2576": {
      "title": "Social Media Officer",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Social Media Officer Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Social Media Officer Apply for job Job reference: 552542 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Brand and Content Closing date: 26/10/2026 School / Directorate: Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment Salary / Grade Grade G (£33,739 - £38,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. Social Media Officer Grade G (£33,739 - £38,825 p.a. pro rata) Full Time/Permanent About the Role We are looking for an experienced, driven and talented social media professional to join our Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) department. The postholder will plan, deliver and implement social media content and campaigns to enhance NTU’s global reputation and support the university’s strategic priorities and objectives. Reporting to the Social Media Manager, the postholder will work collaboratively with teams across CAMS including the Marketing and Campaigns team, School Marketing teams and International Student Recruitment team, producing innovative and engaging content for NTU’s organic social media channels (UK and international). With demonstrable content production and project management skills, you will have a strong track record of creating and editing engaging social media content for specific audiences and experience delivering multi-channel social media campaigns. You’ll be a creative thinker with a keen eye for detail and possess excellent communication and stakeholder management skills along with the ability to manage competing deadlines and priorities. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. About Us Our award-winning Department of Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) is responsible for engaging with key audiences including prospective students to support NTU’s student recruitment targets and driving forward NTU’s reputation and brand. CAMS comprises admissions, applicant engagement, student recruitment events and outreach, international student recruitment, marketing and campaigns, content management, creative services, social media, web and digital, public relations and internal and external communications. If you have a passion for student recruitment, marketing and communications and a drive to make a real difference, CAMS at NTU could be the perfect place for you. In return, we offer you a culture of positivity, encouragement and mutual support. The senior leadership team are committed to nurturing talent and helping people reach their full potential. But most of all, we believe in change and growth; in daring to do things differently. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Katy Law, Social Media Manager, at katy.law@ntu.ac.uk Interview date: 19 November 2026 Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt 552542 - Social Media Officer JDPS (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2562": {
      "title": "Lead Coach - Netball",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lead Coach - Netball Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lead Coach - Netball Apply for job Job reference: 552528 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: NTU Sport Closing date: 31/10/2026 School / Directorate: z.University Sports Activities Salary / Grade See special conditions (Shift work) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. NTU Sport are committed to having 70% of students engaged in sport and physical activity by 2025. Join us on our mission. Lead Coach - Netball Role is paid at £20 per hour Games take place on Wednesday afternoons/ evenings Training is on a Monday evening Please note that delivery will primarily take place during term time About the Role This role will form part of the coaching delivery team for the BUCS Netball program at Nottingham Trent University, one of the top 10 ranked university Netball programs in the country. The role being recruited to will primarily focus on leading on the delivery of all training and matchday provision for our Netball BUCS (2s - 6s) who play in range of Tiers across BUCS. Additionally, you will be instrumental in the selection and retention of talented student athletes, both from within the UK and internationally, along with continuing to develop the thriving and successful performance culture at the heart of the club. With a strong history of delivering coaching to high quality players, you will be instrumental in ensuring that Nottingham Trent University continues to be one of the premier institutions for any student wanting to combine high level Netball with a high quality education. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Proposed interview date: TBC About Us At NTU, we believe that sport is for everyone. That's why we are passionate about creating a welcoming and inclusive environment where our students, staff and the people of Nottingham feel inspired, supported and part of a community. Our core values are Pride, Unity and Respect, and these three pillars are embedded into everything we do at NTU Sport. From the way we deliver coaching and sports science support, to the way we design our world–class facilities, we are committed to developing a culture of inclusivity and respect. Our determination to provide an outstanding service has helped NTU secure multiple BUCS Top 10 finishes across the past decade Our Facilities We have a fantastic range of sports facilities at our City campuses, including industry-standard gym equipment, a 10m climbing wall, a sports hall, dance studios and a sports therapy suite offering physiotherapy and sports massage. Our Clifton campus is home to the Clifton Sports Hub, a fully floodlit 3G Pitch and state of the art all-weather hockey pitch, four grass pitches, three squash courts, an exercise studio, 2 sports halls, and four court tennis centre. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Louise Hopkin (Head of Netball) at louise.hopkin@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us We’ll look after you with ongoing support, good development opportunities and a competitive salary that rewards your contribution. We also offer generous holidays, flexible working options, a pension scheme, great facilities and wide range of savings, discounts and benefits. Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Start to think about your future differently. Apply here. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Work in the UK - GOV.UK Skilled Worker visa, Graduate visa, other work visas, right to work Supporting Documents save_alt 552528 - Lead Coach - Netball JDPS (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2388": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Event Production",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer in Event Production - Lighting (Teaching) Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer in Event Production - Lighting (Teaching) Apply for job Job reference: 552356 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: ART School Office Closing date: 08/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham School of Art & Design Salary / Grade HE Lecturer – TFL (£39,984 - £46,320 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Lecturer in Event Production - Lighting (Teaching) £39,984 - £43,671 per annum (pro rata) Permanent/Part time- 29.6 hours per week About the Role The core purpose of a Teaching-Focused Lecturer is to make a significant contribution to student success through the delivery of high-quality teaching and learning activities within the school. As a key member of the course team, you will contribute to the delivery of modules and course content, helping to ensure students receive an engaging, inclusive and supportive learning experience. You will also support a range of departmental activities, including student recruitment events, departmental meetings and the provision of pastoral support to students. Working closely with course leadership teams, you will help organise teaching resources effectively and play an active role in implementing enhancements to curriculum design and maintaining the school’s high academic standards and excellent student experience and outcomes. You will bring strong subject knowledge, excellent written and verbal communication skills, and confidence in using a range of digital technologies to support learning and teaching. You will be comfortable working both independently and collaboratively and will contribute positively to teaching-related activities across the school. Above all, you will be passionate about supporting students to achieve their potential and succeed in their studies. Lecturer The Lecturer role provides a supportive framework for development and is suitable for a wide range of candidates, including recent graduates and those with limited teaching experience. For candidates who are new to higher education, the focus will be on developing confidence and capability in the delivery of learning and teaching activities, while contributing to the wider student experience and academic community. You will hold a degree in a relevant subject area or possess equivalent professional experience and/or teaching qualifications. For further information, please refer to the attached role profile. We welcome applications from candidates whose experience may not align with every requirement listed. If you are excited by the opportunity and believe you could make a positive contribution, we encourage you to apply. Interview date: W/C 21st September About Us Our Music & Events Department sits at the centre of a vibrant creative community, delivering industry-focused education across performance, production, sound, and live experiences. We prepare the next generation of creative professionals by combining artistic practice, technical expertise and real-world application. Based at our Metronome estate, in the heart of one of the UK’s most dynamic creative cities, students benefit from access to state-of-the-art facilities, including: Professional recording studios and control rooms A large-scale live performance venue and black box space Specialist music and audio production and post-production studios Dedicated rehearsal rooms Live event production and technical facilities, supporting lighting, sound and staging These facilities are designed to replicate professional environments and support experiential learning, ensuring students graduate with the practical skills and confidence to succeed in the music and events industries. Our department brings together musicians, producers, costume and theatre designers, engineers and event professionals in a collaborative and forward-thinking environment. We place a strong emphasis on industry engagement, live briefs and applied learning, working closely with partners across the creative sector to ensure our courses remain relevant, innovative and impactful. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact John Meredith (Head of Department - Music and Events) at John.Meredith@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Safeguarding Statement Nottingham Trent University is committed to safeguarding and promoting the welfare of young people and expects all colleagues to share this commitment. If you are successful, you will be required to undertake an enhanced application and a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check. The post for which you are applying is exempt from Section 4(2) of the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act 1974 requiring any spent convictions to be declared. Any information you provide will be treated in confidence and only used when considering your suitability for the post. Before you apply we recommend you ensure you are able to supply the documentation listed on the DBS website Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2494": {
      "title": "Hourly Paid Lecturer in Computer Science",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Hourly Paid Lecturer in Computer Science Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Hourly Paid Lecturer in Computer Science Apply for job Job reference: 552461 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Computer Science Closing date: 30/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade HPL1 (£39,984- £44,977 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Hourly Paid Lecturer in Computer Science £50.75 per direct hour, this includes 2 or more of the following elements: teaching, preparation and marking of the scheduled programme of work. A flat rate of £20.72 per direct teaching hour will be paid for completing one of the above elements of the schedule. The number of hours required and the days of the week may vary. About the Role You will join the thriving and innovative Departments in our School of Science and Technology which are responsible for teaching and research in a variety of disciplines at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. We are looking for well-rounded academics with experience in the above disciplines, with a positive attitude that wish to be part of a forward looking Department. We are looking for hourly paid lecturers to teach on a range of programmes at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. This vacancy may close at any time once sufficient applications have been received. Early submission of your application is encouraged. For more details, please take a look at the role description and person specification provided below. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: TBC About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our Department of Computer Science combines internationally-significant research with an outstanding record for teaching excellence. Our state-of-the-art facilities and career-focused approach to course design provide the right conditions for students to excel in their chosen fields. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Professor Ahmad Lotfi (Head of Department of Computer Science) , via CMPMgtAdmin@ntu.ac.uk Join Us We can offer you a career with a difference, as together we shape futures, change lives and create the university of the future. Doing things differently, we empower our people to shape, create and innovate. Whether they’re pushing the boundaries with award-winning research, transforming society through global collaborations or supporting and helping our students to achieve their potential. Join our friendly and diverse community of 4,000 professionals, academics and researchers, and you’ll enjoy the support and ownership you need to perform at your best. A great place to work, we value, respect and care for all our colleagues, providing flexible and competitive rewards and genuine opportunities for career progression. So, take on an exciting new challenge with an ambitious university where progress never stops. Safe & Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system, upcoming immigration rules (4th April 2024) changes may impact on eligibility for sponsorship, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. Visit https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa for more information. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2317": {
      "title": "Building Services Technician (HVAC)",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Building Services Technician (HVAC) Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Building Services Technician (HVAC) Apply for job Job reference: 552285 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Energy, Engineering and Maintenance Closing date: 30/10/2026 School / Directorate: Estates and Campus Services Salary / Grade Grade G (£33,739 - £38,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Building Services Technician (HVAC) Salary £33,739 - £38,825 per annum Full time, permanent contract About the Role As a Building Services Technician (HVAC) you will be part of the in-house Estates team that supports and enables the safe, compliant and efficient operation of the university estate. The role is varied and diverse, with day-to-day duties ranging from ensuring that our estate is safe and operational, through to supporting the delivery of key University events such as open days and graduation ceremonies. Typical duties will include: Ensuring the safe and efficient operation of all building mechanical, ventilation and plumbing systems through the management and delivery of preventative planned maintenance, statutory inspections, remedial works and the efficient operation of the systems. Managing specialist contractors, including their procurement, safe delivery of works and performance management. Preparation and evaluation of small works/remedial work tenders, making recommendations with regards to the appointment of contractors and the awarding of works in line with all relevant NTU procurement requirements. Ensuring contract documents and health and safety documents are correctly executed and in place before work commences on site. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. In your supporting statement please clearly outline how you meet the essential and desirable criteria, including examples of past relevant experience. Interview Date: w/c 16th November 2026 About Us Over the past 15 years, we’ve invested more than £450m across our five campuses in Nottingham and Nottinghamshire. Named ‘Modern University of the Year 2023’ by The Times and The Sunday Times, we know that our campuses and facilities are a key part of our success, which is why we’re investing a further £250m across our sites over the next five years. As one of the most environmentally responsible universities in the world, we lead the sector by embedding sustainability into everything we do. As part of our Estates team, you’ll help to guide and support this work by reducing our carbon impact and accelerating our progress to net zero by 2040. Our Estates Our City campus is home to stunning Grade II listed buildings, dynamic architecture and picturesque living walls and terraces. In 2021, our renovation of a former Wesleyan Chapel (University Hall) was recognised as the ‘University Impact Initiative of the Year’ by the Association for University Directors of Estates (AUDE). We continue to invest in sector leading projects with the construction of the Design and Digital Arts building which will open in 2024. Recent developments at our Clifton campus include a £23m Medical Technology Innovation Facility (MTIF), £15m Health and Allied Professions Centre and £1.6m Smart Wireless Innovation Facility (SWIFT). Our Brackenhurst campus offers a veterinary nursing centre, climate-controlled greenhouses, and multiple state-of-the-art laboratories. The Lyth building was completed in 2020 at a cost of £11.5m and offers a wide range of high-quality teaching and social spaces. Our Confetti campus offers access to professional TV, film and music studios, as well as specialist labs, computer suites, industry-standard tech and world class facilities for Esports. From 2023, Confetti will be launching a second site in Whitechapel London, complete with a multipurpose, live events venue. Located at Vision West Nottinghamshire College, our £6.5m Mansfield Hub opened in 2020 and includes state-of-the-art training facilities for clinical practitioners, as well as a sport science laboratory, lecture theatres and flexible study spaces. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Scott Brooks (Head of Engineering, Maintenance and Operations) at scott.brooks@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2271": {
      "title": "Technician Bank Staff",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Technician Bank Staff – Bio-Model Manufacture Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Technician Bank Staff – Bio-Model Manufacture Apply for job Job reference: 552239 Location: City Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Fashion Closing date: 01/06/2027 School / Directorate: Nottingham School of Art & Design Salary / Grade Grade E (£28,063 - £30,185 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Technician Bank Staff - Bio Model Manufacture Salary- £27,246 - £28,608 per annum (pro rata) Hourly paid contract paid on a project-by-project basis About the Role We’re looking for a proactive and skilled individual to join our technical team, supporting the small‑scale production of silicone‑based bio‑models for industry partners and commercial clients. This is an exciting opportunity to work in a growing commercial environment within the Anatomical Replication and Manufacturing department, helping us deliver high‑quality products while contributing to a positive, industry‑focused workplace. In this hands‑on role, you will produce moulds and tools, prepare silicone-based composites, and ensure all materials, equipment and workspaces meet the highest standards. You will take responsibility for tracking material usage, supporting stock procurement, and carrying out routine maintenance to keep the manufacturing area running smoothly. The ideal candidate will be an enthusiastic team player, able to collaborate effectively with colleagues while also working independently when required. You will build and maintain strong internal and external contacts, stay up to date with developments in the field, and ensure Health and Safety regulations are consistently met. If you are organised, practical, and keen to share your skills within an innovative and commercially driven environment, we’d love to hear from you. Apply now and help us shape the future of bio‑model manufacturing. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: w/c 13th July 2026 About Us Our department is pioneering new ways to support surgical training and improve patient outcomes by transforming how surgeons prepare for complex procedures. Traditionally, surgeons have relied on cadavers or real patients to develop their skills, with limited opportunities to practice outside clinical settings. Led by Senior Research Fellow Richard Arm, our team is revolutionising this process through advanced manufacturing and medical modelling. By converting patient scan data into highly realistic 3D‑printed organs that match the exact shape, size and tactile qualities of human tissue, we provide surgeons with an accurate, hands-on platform for rehearsal. These innovations enable clinicians to refine techniques, anticipate challenges, and approach intricate or life‑saving surgeries with greater confidence and reduced risk. Find out more: Biomodels: Anatomical Replication and Manufacturing | Nottingham Trent University For any informal queries about the role please contact Richard Arm at richard.arm@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - we encourage and offer a mixture of office working and working from home. You're empowered to define how you work best for the benefits of your stakeholders. Flexibility - take ownership over how you get your work done. We're open to different working patterns and approaches. 25 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=1569": {
      "title": "Demonstrator in Engineering",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Demonstrator in Engineering Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Demonstrator in Engineering Apply for job Job reference: 551538 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Engineering Closing date: 04/01/2027 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade See special conditions Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Demonstrator in Engineering £14.54 per direct teaching support The number of hours required and the days of the week may vary. About the Role We are seeking to recruit a Laboratory demonstrator, who will be available to work throughout the academic year and will be paid on an hourly basis (up to a maximum of 100 hours per annum). In the Department of Engineering, we provide our students opportunities to gain knowledge and skills through laboratory and seminar sessions in the Engineering Building (Clifton campus). The students are studying a mixture of mechanical, electronics, biomedical and sport subjects. In order to ensure that we provide an excellent student experience we support these sessions with the use of demonstrators who offer support and advice to the students throughout the sessions. You will work under the direction of a module leader and other academics leading the session in delivering high quality demonstrating to undergraduate and/or postgraduate students. Duties will include assisting the academic staff in running the class – offering advice and support to students, liaising with technical staff and marking where required. You must be able to demonstrate excellent interpersonal skills and have the ability to communicate ideas of a complex or technical nature to students effectively, as well as having sound engineering knowledge. Interview date – Ongoing as required Hourly paid Demonstrators are hired throughout the year by the Department of Engineering. Please submit your application to express interest in being added to our demonstrator list. However, your application will not be processed further unless a suitable opportunity arises. About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. In the Department of Engineering we deliver research and teaching in electronic engineering, mechanical engineering, biomedical engineering and sport engineering. We are building a global reputation in areas including human performance and human factors, future materials, biomedical engineering, and robotics. We are working with industrial partners in technology, automotive, aircraft, marine, healthcare engineering, and with sports teams to help them beat world records. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Dr Ben Simpson - ben.simpson@ntu.ac.uk Join Us We can offer you a career with a difference, as together we shape futures, change lives and create the university of the future. Doing things differently, we empower our people to shape, create and innovate. Whether they’re pushing the boundaries with award-winning research, transforming society through global collaborations or supporting and helping our students to achieve their potential. Join our friendly and diverse community of 4,000 professionals, academics and researchers, and you’ll enjoy the support and ownership you need to perform at your best. A great place to work, we value, respect and care for all our colleagues, providing flexible and competitive rewards and genuine opportunities for career progression. So, take on an exciting new challenge with an ambitious university where progress never stops. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. Visit https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa for more information. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt 551538 - Demonstrator Engineering JDPS (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=181": {
      "title": "Short Course Tutor",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Short Course Tutor Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Short Course Tutor Apply for job Job reference: 550150 Location: City Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Not specified Closing date: 01/12/2026 School / Directorate: z.Knowledge Exchange Salary / Grade See special conditions Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Short Course Tutors Experienced tutors and creative professionals are invited to submit proposals for innovative new short courses that will complement our existing portfolio. We are especially interested in those with skills and knowledge in the following themes 3D Modelling and Animation AI Literacy in Creative Practice Creative Branding and Design Idea Generation and Productivity Data Analytics for Creative Businesses Project Management for Creative Professionals Sustainable Design UX and UI Human-Centred Design Video Production. In addition to the above, we also welcome proposals related to creating, making and digital skills in: Architecture and interior design Audience engagement and content creation Creative writing Digital screen arts Fashion, textiles and costume Film and television Fine art Game arts Graphic design and illustration Ideas and innovation Journalism, media, communications and PR Photography Product design. You can read about the courses at www.ntu.ac.uk/creativeshortcourses Short Courses are designed to equip professionals with industry-relevant skills and opportunities to engage directly with current practices and expert practitioners, whilst supporting continuing professional development (CPD) for those looking to upskill or pivot their careers, as well as welcoming enthusiastic learners seeking high-quality creative enrichment and experiences. We also offer a dedicated portfolio of courses tailored specifically for young people aged 15 – 17 years old. To support our international groups, we are also interested to hear from qualified and experienced tutors of English as a Foreign Language. About the Role Short course tutors use their industry experience to help learners navigate specialist creative and digital subjects, providing them with opportunities to maximise their professional or academic development. With an awareness of resources and events in the East Midlands, you will manage and deliver your short course and make a positive impact on the careers of your attendees. You will be able to build rapport with them through an enthusiastic and confident approach to delivery. The courses are fee paying, so a focus on the customer experience and value for money is paramount. You'll receive a management fee for preparing and delivering your short course. This will be discussed and negotiated with the Short Course Manager. For more details, take a look at the role profile. We'll consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements. Next Steps If you have an idea for a short course, apply and submit your proposal as part of your application. You should refer to the guidance document below for support in writing your proposal. You will be required to explain in no more than 200 words the training course you wish to propose. You can put more than one proposal on one application. However, applications received with no proposal will not be considered. Include information on the content that will be covered in the course, who your audience will be and why someone would want to do this course, with a clear explanation of why the subject is relevant today. You can only attach two documents, so we encourage you to upload your proposal in the same document as the Cover Letter, as a Word or PDF document. This advert is part of a rolling recruitment campaign which means applications are reviewed regularly. If your course looks exciting, relevant and innovative, you’ll be invited to meet with the short course team to discuss it in more detail. For informal enquiries please contact Aimee Bollu, Short Course Manager on +44 (0)115 848 2394 or by email at aimee.bollu@ntu.ac.uk. About our Courses We already run an impressive portfolio of short courses that take place during the daytimes, evenings and weekends. Our ambition is to be a widely acknowledged force for good in economic, social and cultural development. We offer a vibrant learning atmosphere that encourages creativity and experimentation in our short course attendees, whether they be professionals enhancing their CV or beginners taking their first steps. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Please note that if your role includes teaching 15 – 17 year olds and as we have cross campus roles available depending on your campus allocation, if successful you may be required to undertake an enhanced application process and a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check. Any information you provide will be treated in confidence and only used when considering your suitability for the post. Supporting Documents save_alt Short Course Proposal Guidance (PDF, KB) save_alt Role Description - Short Course Tutor (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2675": {
      "title": "International Applicant Engagement and Administration Associate",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for International Applicant Engagement and Administration Associate Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results International Applicant Engagement and Administration Associate Apply for job Job reference: 552640 Location: City Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: International Student Recruitment Closing date: 01/11/2026 School / Directorate: Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment Salary / Grade Grade E (£28,063 - £30,185 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. International Applicant Engagement and Administration Associate Salary- £28,063 - £30,185 per annum 9 months Fixed Term Contract (January - September 2027) About the Role An exciting opportunity to join the International team, part of the Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) department at NTU. You will support international students as they make a life changing decision to study in the UK. Working within an experienced team, who will provide training and development, you'll communicate with prospective students all over the world. If you love providing excellent customer service this job will be perfect for you. Using your communication skills through email, phone and other online channels you'll chat with future NTU students to support them as they apply to the university. You'll also work on administration tasks which require excellent attention to detail as you manage important customer information and data. The team has a track record of supporting colleagues to develop in their career - with many previous colleagues progressing from this role within the department. So this is a ideal opportunity if you are a motivated and customer orientated graduate ready to begin your career. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. We welcome internal candidates for secondment opportunities Interview Date: w/c 23rd November 2026 About Us Our award-winning Department of Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) is responsible for engaging with key audiences including prospective students to support NTU’s student recruitment targets and driving forward NTU’s reputation and brand. CAMS comprises admissions, applicant engagement, student recruitment events and outreach, international student recruitment, marketing and campaigns, content management, creative services, social media, web and digital, public relations and internal and external communications. If you have a passion for student recruitment, marketing and communications and a drive to make a real difference, CAMS at NTU could be the perfect place for you. In return, we offer you a culture of positivity, encouragement and mutual support. The senior leadership team are committed to nurturing talent and helping people reach their full potential. But most of all, we believe in change and growth; in daring to do things differently. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Laura Coates (International Administration and Enquiries Officer) at laura.coates@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2722": {
      "title": "Hourly Paid Lecturer",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Hourly Paid Lecturer - Accounting and Finance Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Hourly Paid Lecturer - Accounting and Finance Apply for job Job reference: 552687 Location: City Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Accounting and Finance Closing date: 03/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Business School Salary / Grade HPL1 (£39,984- £44,977 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Empower Future Leaders. Doing things differently. Hourly Paid Lecturer - Accounting and Finance £50.75 per direct teaching hour. This includes 2 or more of the following elements: teaching, preparation and marking of the scheduled programme of work. A flat rate of £20.72 per direct teaching hour will be paid for completing one of the above elements of the schedule. The number of hours required and the days of the week may vary. About the Role We are seeking to recruit hourly paid lecturers who are available to work during the academic year and will be paid on an hourly basis. You will be teaching and supporting undergraduates and postgraduate students across the range of courses. We are looking for people with expertise in any of the following areas: Financial and Management Accounting Corporate Finance and Financial Management Taxation Corporate Governance Risk Management For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interviews: 9th November 2026 For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. About Us Nottingham Business School (NBS) delivers research and education that combine academic excellence with real-world impact on people, business, and society. We lead in experiential learning and personalised education, and our research drives positive change across social and economic spheres. This informs all our programmes, from undergraduate to doctoral. With strong partnerships across business, public, and voluntary sectors, NBS is known as the business school for business . We hold the prestigious Triple Crown Accreditation (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA), placing us in the top 1% of business schools worldwide. Discover more on our website . At NTU, we do things differently. Join one of Europe’s largest and most innovative business schools to help shape inclusive research and make a real difference. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact please contact Vangelis Tsiligkiris (Head of Accounting and Finance Department) at vangelis.tsiligiris@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe & Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2709": {
      "title": "Hourly Paid Lecturer in Applied Linguistics",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Hourly Paid Lecturer in Applied Linguistics Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Hourly Paid Lecturer in Applied Linguistics Apply for job Job reference: 552674 Location: City Campus Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Nottingham Institute of Languages and Intercultural Communication Closing date: 18/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Social Sciences Salary / Grade HPL1 (£39,984- £44,977 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Hourly Paid Lecturer - (Linguistics) £50.75 per direct teaching hour. This includes 2 or more of the following elements: teaching, preparation and marking of the scheduled programme of work. A flat rate of £20.72 per direct teaching hour will be paid for completing one of the above elements of the schedule. The number of hours required and the days of the week may vary. About the Role We are looking for a colleague who can contribute to the delivery of selected modules on our BA English Language and Linguistics and our MA TESOL. We are particularly interested in applicants with teaching and research expertise in corpus-based approaches and competence in the teaching of research methods (including quantitative and qualitative methods). For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. The School of Social Sciences at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is recognised nationally and internationally for delivering theoretically informed and applied leanring, teaching, and research. We foster a culture that values the diversity of all our communities and publicises and celebrates excellence in all we do. The Nottingham Institute of Languages and Intercultural Communications is a diverse, supportive, and collaborative community in which to innovate, explore and create. Our specialities span across a range of subject areas, including Applied Linguistics, English language teaching, foreign language learning, Academic English, and Intercultural Communication. We maintain a vibrant and inclusive international learning and teaching environment that is grounded in scholarship, research, and professional practice. Our courses are built on the ethos of developing intellectual and practical skills, adding value to students’ employability and providing an outstanding student experience. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Associate Professor David Wright at david.wright @ntu.ac.uk . Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2691": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer CSI",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer / Senior Lecturer CSI Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer / Senior Lecturer CSI Apply for job Job reference: 552656 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Chemistry and Forensics Closing date: 05/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade HE Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (£39,984 - £58,624 pa pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse community. Inclusive Research. Rewarding Careers. Doing things differently. Lecturer/Senior Lecturer Crime Scene Investigation HE Lecturer £39,984 - £43,671 per annum (pro rata) Part time (0.7 FTE) About the Role Join our ambitious and highly regarded Forensic Science team and help shape the next generation of crime scene investigators. Whether your experience comes from industry, academia, or a combination of both, you will play a key role in delivering an outstanding student experience across our accredited undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. In this role, you will: Teach and support students across a range of forensic science and crime scene investigation modules. Share your expertise in crime scene processing, crime scene management, and related professional practice. Design and deliver engaging learning experiences through laboratories, workshops, seminars, field activities, and research projects. Develop teaching materials and contribute to the continual enhancement of our curriculum. Assess student work, provide constructive feedback, and support student progression and success. Contribute to the management, quality assurance, and ongoing development of our forensic science courses. Undertake research, scholarly, pedagogic, or professional practice activities that enhance your subject expertise and inform teaching. Work collaboratively with colleagues to maintain the high standards expected of programmes accredited by the Chartered Society of Forensic Sciences. You will be part of a department committed to innovation, student success, and professional relevance. Our Forensic Science programmes are recognised among the UK's top five courses in the subject area, providing an exciting environment in which to develop your academic and professional career. If you are passionate about forensic science, enjoy inspiring students, and want to help develop future practitioners, we would love to hear from you. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our industry-standard Forensic Science facilities and equipment support our teaching and research and they are also used regularly by external organisations. Our crime scene training facility is one of the largest in the UK and is regularly used for teaching, training and research. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Rachel Bolton King (Courses Manager Forensic Science) at rachel.bolton-king@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=430": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Senior Research Fellow Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Senior Research Fellow Apply for job Job reference: 550399 Location: City Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Masters and Legal Research Closing date: 31/10/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Law School Salary / Grade Grade I (£49,127 - £58,624 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Senior Research Fellow in Law Salary £49,127 - £58,624 per annum (pro rata) Part time- 7.4 hours per week/ Fixed term for 6 months About the Role Would you like your research to help improve how public inquiries work across the UK? As a Senior Research Fellow in Nottingham Law School, you will support the delivery of a programme of work designed to improve the effectiveness, impact and value of public inquiries and strengthen their contribution to learning, policy development and organisational change. Working closely with the project lead, you will contribute to research, stakeholder engagement and project delivery activities. You will monitor developments across public inquiries and identify procedural, operational and reporting issues relevant to the project. You will engage with inquiry chairs, secretaries, practitioners, policymakers, advocacy groups and other stakeholders, coordinate participation in interviews, focus groups and other project work, quality-assure materials, identify emerging themes, and contribute to the planning, coordination and delivery of the project. Throughout, you will exercise sound judgement, work collaboratively, and maintain high standards of confidentiality, research ethics and data protection. This is a 0.2 FTE role, equivalent to 7.4 hours per week. It offers an opportunity to contribute to a focused, policy-relevant programme of work and support practical resources that can promote learning and improvement across UK public inquiries. Interview w/c 16th October 2026 About Us Nottingham Law School (NLS) is one of the leading providers of academic and professional legal education in the country, with an established record of delivering innovative and transformational courses. We are one of the largest law schools in the UK, offering a range of undergraduate degrees, academic and practitioner taught postgraduate courses and a strong research degrees programme. In addition, our students can gain practical experience volunteering at NLS Legal, our multi-award-winning-teaching law firm, the only on-campus law firm at a UK Law School. Our School has built a reputation for excellence in the provision of legal education and in shaping the careers of solicitors, barristers and legal practitioners at both national and international levels. In addition to our outstanding research expertise, we have long established links with policy makers, professional bodies and leading law firms, including a growing number of significant international associations. We have an extensive record of delivering excellent bespoke training programmes for practitioners and professional bodies, and have strengths in commissioned research, both in the UK and overseas. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Associate Professor Dr Emma Ireton emma.ireton@ntu.ac.uk Join Us 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Hybrid working - we encourage and offer a mixture of office working and working from home. You're empowered to define how you work best for the benefits of your stakeholders. Flexibility - take ownership over how you get your work done. We're open to different working patterns and approaches. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2597": {
      "title": "School Research Administrator",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for School Research Administrator Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results School Research Administrator Apply for job Job reference: 552562 Location: City Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: NBS School Office Closing date: 06/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Business School Salary / Grade Grade E (£28,063 - £30,185 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Empower Future Leaders. Doing things differently. School Research Administrator Salary- £28,063 - £30,185 per annum (pro rata) This is a part time role (6 hours a day, 4 days a week)/ Fixed term for 1 year About the Role We have an exciting opportunity to join the School Management Support Team at Nottingham Business School as a part-time School Research Administrator (24 hours per week) . This is a one-year fixed-term role supporting the School's thriving research community and contributing to the delivery of a professional, efficient and high-quality administration service. The role will be based at our City Campus and will involve a mix of on-campus and remote home working. As a School Research Administrator, you will provide comprehensive administrative support to the Heads of Research Centres and work with Research Centre staff to ensure effective administration of our Research Groups. You will play a key role in the organisation and administration of research programmes, acting as a central point of contact for academic colleagues, research students and a range of internal and external stakeholders. A commitment to delivering excellent customer service and support is essential. The role offers a varied workload and will involve supporting research events and training activities, managing research student administration processes, coordinating meetings and committees, maintaining records and databases, and liaising with colleagues across the University, including the Doctoral School. You will also contribute to activities that support the School's research objectives, accreditation activity and postgraduate research experience. Please submit a supporting statement of no more than 1,000 words demonstrating how you meet the requirements of the School Research Administrator role. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: w/c 16th November 2026 About Us Nottingham Business School (NBS) delivers research and education that combine academic excellence with real-world impact on people, business, and society. We lead in experiential learning and personalised education, and our research drives positive change across social and economic spheres. This informs all our programmes, from undergraduate to doctoral. With strong partnerships across business, public, and voluntary sectors, NBS is known as the business school for business . We hold the prestigious Triple Crown Accreditation (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA), placing us in the top 1% of business schools worldwide. Discover more on our website . At NTU, we do things differently. Join one of Europe’s largest and most innovative business schools to help shape inclusive research and make a real difference. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact John Moore (School Coordinator) at john.moore@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- School Research Administrator (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2678": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Forensics Science",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Forensics Science Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Forensics Science Apply for job Job reference: 552643 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Chemistry and Forensics Closing date: 28/10/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade HE Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (£39,984 - £58,624 pa pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Diverse community. Inclusive Research. Rewarding Careers. Doing things differently. Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Forensics Science Lecturer Salary- £39,984- £43,671 per annum Senior Lecturer Salary- £46,320- £58,624 per annum Full time/ Fixed term for 9 months About the Role The Department of Physical Sciences is seeking to appoint an enthusiastic and ambitious Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Forensic Science to join our thriving academic community on a fixed-term basis for nine months. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to the delivery and continued development of our accredited undergraduate and postgraduate forensic science programmes while advancing your own research, scholarship, or professional practice. We are looking for a passionate educator who can inspire students through innovative, evidence-based teaching and provide an outstanding learning experience. You will contribute to teaching, assessment and curriculum development, across our forensic science portfolio, while also supporting teaching more broadly within the department. We welcome applications from candidates with academic, industrial, or practitioner backgrounds. We are particularly interested in individuals with expertise in one or more of the following areas: Marks and traces evidence The English legal system and the role of forensic science within criminal justice ISO standards and quality management within forensic practice Forensic biology You will join a collaborative team of experienced practitioners and academics committed to delivering an excellent student experience and maintaining high professional standards. Our forensic science programmes are recognised among the top-performing in the UK (Complete University Guide), providing students with a strong blend of scientific knowledge, practical skills, and professional relevance. The successful candidate will demonstrate a proactive and collegiate approach, a commitment to educational excellence, and the ability to contribute to the continued growth and success of the subject area. Whether you are an established academic seeking your next challenge or a forensic professional looking to transition into higher education, we would welcome your application. This nine-month fixed-term appointment offers an excellent opportunity to join a supportive and high-performing team and help shape the next generation of forensic scientists. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. Interview Date: w/c 9th November 2026 About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our industry-standard Forensic Science facilities and equipment support our teaching and research and they are also used regularly by external organisations. Our crime scene training facility is one of the largest in the UK and is regularly used for teaching, training and research. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Emma Rixon (Head of Department) at emma.rixon@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2719": {
      "title": "School Marketing Executive",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for School Marketing Executive Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results School Marketing Executive Apply for job Job reference: 552684 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Marketing - School Closing date: 15/11/2026 School / Directorate: Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment Salary / Grade Grade F (£29,352 - £33,739 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. School Marketing Executive Salary- £29,352 - £33,739 per annum Permanent / Full time About the Role We're looking for a creative, proactive and digitally-focused marketing professional to join Nottingham School of Art & Design's marketing team as a School Marketing Executive. Working as part of Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS), you'll support the delivery of integrated marketing campaigns and student recruitment activity that enhances the profile and reputation of Nottingham School of Art & Design and helps attract prospective students across undergraduate and postgraduate audiences. You'll also support activity promoting NTU London and across Schools where required. Reporting to the Senior School Marketing Manager, you'll play an important role in creating engaging content and delivering campaigns across a range of channels, including web, email, social media, digital advertising and events. From developing student stories and case studies to supporting open days, recruitment events and conversion activity, you'll help bring the NTU experience to life for prospective students. We're looking for someone with a good understanding of digital marketing principles, and experience delivering marketing activity in a customer-focused environment. You'll be confident building relationships with a wide range of stakeholders, managing multiple priorities and using insight and performance data to continually improve your work. This is an exciting opportunity to join a collaborative and ambitious team, working on campaigns that make a real difference to student recruitment and help shape the future of one of the UK's leading creative schools. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: 24th November 2026 About Us Our award-winning Department of Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) is responsible for engaging with key audiences including prospective students to support NTU’s student recruitment targets and driving forward NTU’s reputation and brand. CAMS comprises admissions, applicant engagement, student recruitment events and outreach, international student recruitment, marketing and campaigns, content management, creative services, social media, web and digital, public relations and internal and external communications. If you have a passion for student recruitment, marketing and communications and a drive to make a real difference, CAMS at NTU could be the perfect place for you. In return, we offer you a culture of positivity, encouragement and mutual support. The senior leadership team are committed to nurturing talent and helping people reach their full potential. But most of all, we believe in change and growth; in daring to do things differently. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact James Tissiman-Foster at james.tissiman-foster@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe & Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- School Marketing Executive (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2726": {
      "title": "Veterinary Nursing Centre Assistant Co-Ordinator",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Veterinary Nursing Centre Assistant Co-Ordinator Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Veterinary Nursing Centre Assistant Co-Ordinator Apply for job Job reference: 552691 Location: Brackenhurst Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Animal and Environmental Sciences Closing date: 10/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Animal Rural and Environmental Sciences Salary / Grade Grade F (£29,352 - £33,739 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Making a Positive Impact, Together. Doing things differently. Veterinary Nursing Centre Assistant Co-Ordinator Salary- £29,352 - £33,739 per annum Full time/ Permanent About the Role Are you an RVN or MRCVS who enjoys supporting and developing the next generation of veterinary professionals? We have an exciting opportunity to join our Veterinary Nursing Centre Placement Team at NTU. Working as part of our Veterinary Nursing Technical Team, you’ll play an important role in supporting students as they develop their clinical skills, confidence and professional experience. The role offers a great mix of hands-on student support and placement activity, including practical demonstrations, training practice visits, placement support and quality assurance of Nursing Progress Logs (NPLs). You’ll also work closely with colleagues and veterinary professionals, building strong internal and external networks that help us provide an engaging, relevant learning experience and prepare our students for successful careers. If you’re passionate about veterinary nursing and would enjoy using your clinical experience to support, encourage and inspire students, we’d love to hear from you. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: w/c 23rd November 2026 About Us We are the School of Animal, Rural and Environmental Science (ARES) at Nottingham Trent University. Our business is nature: specifically, the environment, animal health and welfare, ecology and conservation, and agriculture and food production.. Our approach is innovative and inclusive. We feel it makes us that little bit different. It’s our goal to have a positive impact on the planet by improving the well being of environments, animals, plants, and people. If you see that passion in yourself, we can be a new, powerful partner in your career. For any informal queries about the role or the ARES team, please contact Rich Plant (School Technical Manager) at richard.plant@ntua.cuk@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2705": {
      "title": "Senior Marketing Manager (Corporate and Brand)",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Senior Marketing Manager (Corporate and Brand) Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Senior Marketing Manager (Corporate and Brand) Apply for job Job reference: 552670 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Marketing - Central Closing date: 15/11/2026 School / Directorate: Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment Salary / Grade Grade I (£49,127 - £58,624 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Be part of something bigger. Doing things differently. Senior Marketing Manager (Corporate and Brand) Salary- £49,127 - £58,624 per annum Full time/Permanent About the Role We're looking for an experienced and strategic marketing leader to oversee NTU's corporate, brand and content marketing activity, strengthening our reputation and engagement with key audiences. You'll lead a broad portfolio of activity spanning corporate campaigns, brand development, content strategy and stakeholder engagement. Working with colleagues across the University, you'll develop integrated marketing and communications that support organisational priorities and showcase NTU's strengths and impact, with a particular focus on business and employer engagement. You'll bring a strong track record of leading insight-led marketing activity and delivering high-profile campaigns for external audiences. You'll be skilled at building effective stakeholder relationships and ensuring communications are clear, consistent and impactful across multiple audiences and channels. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: Monday 30 November About Us Our award-winning Department of Communications, Alumni Relations, Marketing and Student Recruitment (CAMS) is responsible for engaging with key audiences including prospective students to support NTU’s student recruitment targets and driving forward NTU’s reputation and brand. CAMS comprises admissions, applicant engagement, student recruitment events and outreach, international student recruitment, marketing and campaigns, content management, creative services, social media, web and digital, public relations and internal and external communications. If you have a passion for student recruitment, marketing and communications and a drive to make a real difference, CAMS at NTU could be the perfect place for you. In return, we offer you a culture of positivity, encouragement and mutual support. The senior leadership team are committed to nurturing talent and helping people reach their full potential. But most of all, we believe in change and growth; in daring to do things differently. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Dani Hulse , Head of Marketing and Campaigns at dani.hulse@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Applications from job seekers who require sponsorship to work in the UK are welcome and will be considered alongside all other applications. Whilst this role is currently eligible for sponsorship under the Skilled Worker Route, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- Senior Marketing Manager (Corporate and Brand) (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2530": {
      "title": "Professor and Head of Department in Accounting and Finance",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Professor and Head of Department in Accounting and Finance Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Professor and Head of Department in Accounting and Finance Apply for job Job reference: 552496 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Accounting and Finance Closing date: 20/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Business School Salary / Grade Management Grade 2 (£75,000 -  £91,000 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Empower Future Leaders. Doing things differently. Professor and Head of Accounting and Finance Salary £75,000 - £95,000 per annum Full time/Permanent About the Role At Nottingham Business School (NBS), we are committed to delivering education and research that combine academic excellence with positive impact on people, business and society. As a Triple Crown business school, we are one of the top business schools in the world, and proud of our collaborative culture, ambitious outlook. Through world-leading research, industry engagement and innovative and immersive education, we empower our students and staff to shape a more sustainable, inclusive and prosperous future. NBS has a strong reputation for excellence in teaching, research and business engagement, we are committed to continually enhancing our academic offer and ensuring our graduates are equipped to thrive in a rapidly changing global environment. We are looking to appoint a Head of Department of Accounting and Finance and Professor to provide strategic leadership and direction for to further develop our research and education that matters to business and the world. The successful candidate will play a key role in delivering the NBS’ and NTU’s strategic objectives, leading on academic excellence, research and knowledge exchange, student experience, and external engagement across the Accounting and Finance portfolio. The Department of Accounting and Finance delivers an extensive portfolio of undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral programmes. Our courses are informed by state-of-the-art research, industry practice and strong links with professional bodies and employers, ensuring graduates develop the knowledge, skills and experience required to succeed in an increasingly dynamic global economy. As Head of Department and a key member of the NBS and NTU leadership, you will lead a talented community of academics, helping to further strengthen the department's reputation for excellence in teaching, research, professional engagement and student experience. As a professor you will lead impactful and excellent research in your field and shape the future of accounting and finance. You will be a proven academic leader and excellent communicator with a passion for innovation in higher education, outstanding student outcomes, and the advancement of research and professional practice. Working collaboratively with members of the School Executive Team and reporting directly to the Executive Dean of Nottingham Business School, you will contribute to the strategic development of the NBS whilst leading and inspiring colleagues within the department. You will be responsible for ensuring the continued success and growth of the department, fostering a culture of excellence in education, research and collaboration with business, professional bodies, employers, alumni and other external stakeholders. In this senior academic leadership role with significant line management responsibilities, you will possess outstanding academic reputation, leadership and people management skills, alongside substantial experience within higher education and a strong understanding of contemporary issues affecting accounting and finance education, research and professional practice. Join the Department of Accounting and Finance at Nottingham Business School and play a leading role in shaping our research, academic community and external impact. We welcome applications from established academics across all areas of accounting and finance . We are particularly interested in expertise that complements our strategic priorities, including financial reporting, corporate governance, and the implications of digital technologies and data analytics for accounting and finance. We would welcome application from both professorial and non-professorial academic applicants. As Professor of Accounting and Finance, you will: Lead internationally recognised research , producing high-quality publications and helping shape the research agenda in your field. Grow our research community , mentoring colleagues, building collaborative research activity and supporting an inclusive and ambitious research culture. Develop our doctoral community , supervising PhD researchers and contributing to doctoral training and development. Secure and lead external funding , developing major research and knowledge-exchange projects with funders, professional bodies, industry and international partners. Create meaningful impact , translating research into benefits for policy, professional practice, business and society. Bring your expertise into education , contributing to undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral teaching and helping shape innovative, research-informed curricula. Provide academic leadership , contributing to the strategic development of the Department and School and strengthening our national and international profile. You will have the opportunity to influence the future direction of Accounting and Finance at Nottingham Business School while developing ambitious research, partnerships and people. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview date: Monday 30th November 2026 About Us Nottingham Business School (NBS) delivers research and education that combine academic excellence with real-world impact on people, business, and society. We lead in experiential learning and personalised education, and our research drives positive change across social and economic spheres. This informs all our programmes, from undergraduate to doctoral. With strong partnerships across business, public, and voluntary sectors, NBS is known as the business school for business . We hold the prestigious Triple Crown Accreditation (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA), placing us in the top 1% of business schools worldwide. Discover more on our website . At NTU, we do things differently. Join one of Europe’s largest and most innovative business schools to help shape inclusive research and make a real difference. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Professor Baback Yazdani, Executive Dean of Nottingham Business School, at baback.yazdani@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 35 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Annual Health Insurance or Private Medical Insurance Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2706": {
      "title": "Hourly Paid Lecturer in Forensics",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Hourly Paid Lecturer in Forensics Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Hourly Paid Lecturer in Forensics Apply for job Job reference: 552671 Location: All NTU Campuses Employment type: Hourly Paid/Casual Contract Team: Chemistry and Forensics Closing date: 04/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade HPL1 (£39,984- £44,977 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Hourly Paid Lecturer in Forensic Science £50.75 per direct hour, this includes 2 or more of the following elements: teaching, preparation and marking of the scheduled programme of work. A flat rate of £20.72 per direct teaching hour will be paid for completing one of the above elements of the schedule. The number of hours required and the days of the week may vary. About the Role This is an opportunity to join our Department of Physical Sciences, within the Forensic Science team, and contribute to the delivery of high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate teaching. We are seeking an enthusiastic and knowledgeable academic with expertise in one or more of the following areas: crime scene investigation; legal and regulatory frameworks in Forensic Science. You will prepare and deliver engaging teaching, develop learning materials, and support student learning through a range of teaching, assessment, and feedback activities. The role includes setting and marking coursework, projects, dissertations, and examinations, providing constructive feedback, and supporting students throughout their academic journey. As part of a collaborative academic community, you will contribute to programme delivery, attend course and team meetings, and undertake related administrative and pastoral responsibilities. You will be expected to maintain accurate student records and work closely with academic, technical, administrative, and professional services colleagues to ensure an excellent student experience. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to high-quality teaching, student support, and continuous professional development, ensuring their subject knowledge remains current and informed by developments in the discipline. This is a varied and rewarding role offering the opportunity to make a direct impact on student success while contributing to the continued development of our Forensic Science provision. The balance of responsibilities will be agreed with the successful candidate and their line manager, reflecting both individual expertise and departmental needs. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: 12th November 2026 About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing, engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our industry-standard Forensic Science facilities and equipment support our teaching and research. They are also used regularly by external organisations. Our crime scene training facility is one of the largest in the UK and is used for teaching, training and research. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Dr Matt Tranter (Interim Deputy Head of Department) at Matt.Tranter@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us We’ll look after you with ongoing support, good development opportunities and a competitive salary that rewards your contribution. We also offer generous holidays, flexible working options, a pension scheme, great facilities and wide range of savings, discounts and benefits. Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University Start to think about your future differently. Apply here. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2721": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer / Senior Lecturer Occupational Therapy Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer / Senior Lecturer Occupational Therapy Apply for job Job reference: 552686 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care Closing date: 18/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Social Sciences Salary / Grade HE Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (£39,984 - £58,624 pa pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Inspire, drive change and save lives. Doing things differently. Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer in Occupational Therapy Lecturer Salary- £39,984- £43,671 per annum Senior Lecturer Salary- £46,320- £58,624 per annum Full time/Permanent About the Role The Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care at Nottingham Trent University is looking to appoint an enthusiastic and forward-thinking Occupational Therapy Lecturer/Senior Lecturer to join our academic team. We’re seeking an individual who is experienced in the field of Occupational Therapy and who can provide high quality teaching and learning for our students. The successful candidate will join the Occupational Therapy team to make a valued contribution to our newly established Occupational Therapy courses. You will participate in the planning, delivery, assessment, and quality assurance processes across the BSc and MSc programmes. You will contribute to student recruitment for both the courses. You will act as a personal tutor for Occupational Therapy students, providing pastoral care, working collaboratively with our key stakeholder organisations to ensure support and high-quality learning experiences for students. The successful candidate will have experience working with learners in practice or higher education, designing, and delivering learning opportunities, and have a good understanding of current and evolving clinical, professional, and policy developments in Occupational Therapy. You will possess excellent communication skills with a willingness to continue developing your scholarly, practice, or research profile. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: Thursday 26th November 2026 About Us Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care brings together expert and enthusiastic staff from across the health, social care, and social work sectors, many of whom are experienced practitioners and recognised leaders in their fields. Our academics are actively engaged in research and scholarship, with work that is widely published and directly informs our curriculum, ensuring students benefit from a contemporary, evidence-based and professionally relevant learning experience. We are committed to providing a vibrant, inclusive and supportive learning environment where teaching is grounded in research, professional practice and a strong commitment to student success. By fostering collaboration between students, practitioners, researchers and external partners, we prepare graduates to make a meaningful impact within their professions and communities. The Institute is dedicated to developing innovative education and research that addresses the challenges facing health and social care services today. Through our strong partnerships with healthcare, social care and community organisations, we strive to make a positive contribution to improving health, wellbeing and social outcomes for all. Our ambition is to equip the next generation of professionals with the knowledge, skills and values needed to lead change and improve lives in an evolving health and social care landscape. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Principal Lecturer Carl Webster Carl.Webster@ntu.ac.uk or Academic Director Anne Felton Anne.Felton@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2652": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Children's Nursing",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Senior Lecturer in Children&#39;s Nursing Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Senior Lecturer in Children's Nursing Apply for job Job reference: 552617 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care Closing date: 09/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Social Sciences Salary / Grade Grade I (£49,127 - £58,624 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Inspire, drive change and save lives. Doing things differently. Senior Lecturer in Children's Nursing Salary- £49,127 - £58,624 per annum Full time/ permanent About the Role The Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care at Nottingham Trent University is looking to appoint an enthusiastic and forward-thinking senior lecturer in Children’s Nursing to join our academic team. We are seeking an individual who is experienced in the field of Children’s Nursing and who can provide high-quality teaching and learning for our students. The successful candidate will join our dynamic and future focused Nursing Team to make a valued contribution to our range of pre-registration undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. and continuing professional development courses. You will be supporting the development and delivery of our newly established Children's Nursing programme. While the primary focus of the role is Children's Nursing, there will be opportunities to collaborate with all four fields of nursing, supporting innovation, curriculum development, and an exceptional student experience. You will participate in the recruitment, planning, delivery, assessment, and quality assurance processes across nursing programmes. You will act as a personal tutor and academic assessor for nursing students, and work collaboratively with our key stakeholder organisations to ensure support and high-quality learning experiences. You will also hold leadership positions within the course team. The successful candidate will have experience working with learners in higher education, designing, delivering and evaluating innovative learning opportunities. Applicants should demonstrate a scholarly, practice, or research profile, together with an excellent understanding of current and evolving clinical, professional, and policy developments relevant to children's nursing. As an applicant, you will possess excellent communication skills and have experience in working collaboratively across teams to support high-quality learning environments. You should bring experience of curriculum development and of leadership within a higher education context. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: w/c 23rd November 2026 About Us Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care brings together expert and enthusiastic staff from across the health, social care, and social work sectors, many of whom are experienced practitioners and recognised leaders in their fields. Our academics are actively engaged in research and scholarship, with work that is widely published and directly informs our curriculum, ensuring students benefit from a contemporary, evidence-based and professionally relevant learning experience. We are committed to providing a vibrant, inclusive and supportive learning environment where teaching is grounded in research, professional practice and a strong commitment to student success. By fostering collaboration between students, practitioners, researchers and external partners, we prepare graduates to make a meaningful impact within their professions and communities. The Institute is dedicated to developing innovative education and research that addresses the challenges facing health and social care services today. Through our strong partnerships with healthcare, social care and community organisations, we strive to make a positive contribution to improving health, wellbeing and social outcomes for all. Our ambition is to equip the next generation of professionals with the knowledge, skills and values needed to lead change and improve lives in an evolving health and social care landscape. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Laura Holliday , Associate Professor, Children’s Nursing at Laura.Holliday@ntu.ac.uk or Anne Felton Director of Institute of Health and Social Care at Anne.Felton@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Applications from job seekers who require sponsorship to work in the UK are welcome and will be considered alongside all other applications. Whilst this role is currently eligible for sponsorship under the Skilled Worker Route, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2607": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Operations, Analytics, and Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Associate Professor in Operations, Analytics, and Artificial Intelligence Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Associate Professor in Operations, Analytics, and Artificial Intelligence Apply for job Job reference: 552572 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Strategy, Analytics and Operations Closing date: 15/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Business School Salary / Grade Grade J (£60,377 - £69,962 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Empower Future Leaders. Doing things differently. Associate Professor in Operations, Analytics, and Artificial Intelligence Salary- £60,377 - £69,962 per annum Full time/ Permanent About the Role The Department of Strategy, Analytics and Operations at Nottingham Business School is actively looking for an enthusiastic and motivated individual to join us as Associate Professor in Operations, Analytics and Artificial Intelligence. We are seeking a candidate who can contribute to the research and learning culture through research leadership, capacity and curriculum development within the subject area. The ideal candidate should have a strong research profile and expertise in one or more of the following areas: digital technologies and AI for sustainable operations, business intelligence and data management, responsible AI and governance, AI strategy, or AI-enabled transformation. This role is diverse, providing opportunities to contribute to a wide range of collaborative research and teaching-related activities across all levels. Responsibilities include engaging in the Department's Sustainable Operations and Analytics Research Lab as well as working closely with colleagues across the department to support the school's research and learning strategy. Additionally, the role offers the chance for individuals to utilise their knowledge in designing academic content for students. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. Interview Date: Week commencing 30/11/2026. About Us Nottingham Business School (NBS) delivers research and education that combine academic excellence with real-world impact on people, business, and society. We lead in experiential learning and personalised education, and our research drives positive change across social and economic spheres. This informs all our programmes, from undergraduate to doctoral. With strong partnerships across business, public, and voluntary sectors, NBS is known as the business school for business. We hold the prestigious Triple Crown Accreditation (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA), placing us in the top 1% of business schools worldwide. Discover more on our website . At NTU, we do things differently. Join one of Europe’s largest and most innovative business schools to help shape inclusive research and make a real difference. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact either Demola Obembe – Head of Department at demola.obembe@ntu.ac.uk or Michael Hewitt – Assistant Head of Department at michael.hewitt@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Applications from job seekers who require sponsorship to work in the UK are welcome and will be considered alongside all other applications. Whilst this role is currently eligible for sponsorship under the Skilled Worker Route, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2529": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Accounting and Finance",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Accounting and Finance Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Accounting and Finance Apply for job Job reference: 552495 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Accounting and Finance Closing date: 16/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Business School Salary / Grade HE Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (£39,984 - £58,624 pa pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Empower Future Leaders. Doing things differently. Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Accounting and Finance Lecturer Salary- £39,984 - £43,671 per annum Senior Lecturer Salary- £46,320- £58,624 per annum Full time/Permanent About the Role Join the Department of Accounting and Finance at Nottingham Business School and help us deliver an outstanding, relevant and inclusive learning experience for our students. We are recruiting across a range of Accounting and Finance specialisms and are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: financial management, corporate finance, digital finance, taxation, audit, financial accounting and corporate governance . As a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer, you will teach and support students across our undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. You will lead and contribute to modules, supervise projects and dissertations, provide effective feedback, and help ensure our courses remain current and responsive to developments in the profession and industry. You will have opportunities to: Bring your subject expertise into the classroom , using engaging and innovative approaches to teaching, learning and assessment. Shape our curriculum , contributing to module and course development, review, accreditation and quality enhancement. Support our students , helping them achieve their academic and professional ambitions. Develop your research, scholarship and/or professional practice , using this activity to inform your teaching and contribute to wider impact. Build external connections , working with professional bodies, industry and national or international partners. Contribute to our academic community , working collaboratively with colleagues and, depending on your experience, taking on module, course or other academic leadership responsibilities. You will join a supportive academic team where you can develop your expertise, contribute new ideas and play an active role in the continued development of Accounting and Finance at Nottingham Business School. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: w/c 23rd November 2026 About Us Nottingham Business School (NBS) delivers research and education that combine academic excellence with real-world impact on people, business, and society. We lead in experiential learning and personalised education, and our research drives positive change across social and economic spheres. This informs all our programmes, from undergraduate to doctoral. With strong partnerships across business, public, and voluntary sectors, NBS is known as the business school for business . We hold the prestigious Triple Crown Accreditation (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA), placing us in the top 1% of business schools worldwide. Discover more on our website . At NTU, we do things differently. Join one of Europe’s largest and most innovative business schools to help shape inclusive research and make a real difference. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Vangelis Tsiligkiris (Head of Department, Accounting and Finance) at vangelis.tsiligkiris@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2718": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Nonlinear Photonics",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Research Fellow in Nonlinear Photonics Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Research Fellow in Nonlinear Photonics Apply for job Job reference: 552683 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Engineering Closing date: 06/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Science and Technology Salary / Grade Grade H (£39,984 - £44,977 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Research Fellow in Nonlinear Photonics £39,984 - £44,977 p.a. pro rata Full time/Fixed Term - 2 years starting on 1st January 2027 (with the potential of extension). About the role We are seeking a Research Fellow to join an exciting European Research Council funded project focused on nonlinear nanophotonics and nonlinear metasurface-enabled spectroscopy and imaging in the Advanced Optics and Photonics (AOP) Group. The research will explore how engineered optical resonances and nonlinear light-matter interactions can enable new approaches to near-infrared detection, optical frequency conversion and computational imaging. You will undertake innovative experimental and simulation-based research, contributing to the development of new knowledge in nonlinear nanophotonics, metasurfaces and optical spectroscopy. Key activities will include electromagnetic modelling, developing optical setups, measuring linear and nonlinear optical responses, and implementing imaging and image-reconstruction techniques. The work will investigate resonantly enhanced nonlinear processes, including harmonic generation and frequency mixing, and their application to wavelength conversion and the recovery of spatial and spectral information. You will contribute to research planning, data analysis, publications, conference presentations and future funding applications. You will also support the wider research environment through collaboration with academic partners, supervision of student projects and occasional teaching of research methods and techniques. This is an excellent opportunity to develop your research profile while contributing to a cutting-edge area of photonics research. Interview date: w/c 16th November About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. In the Department of Engineering we deliver research and teaching in electronic engineering, mechanical engineering, biomedical engineering and sport engineering. We are building a global reputation in areas including human performance and human factors, future materials, biomedical engineering, and robotics. We are working with industrial partners in technology, automotive, aircraft, marine, healthcare engineering, and with sports teams to help them beat world records. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Dr. Lei Xu at lei.xu@ntu.ac.uk Join Us 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Hybrid working - we encourage and offer a mixture of office working and working from home. You're empowered to define how you work best for the benefits of your stakeholders. Flexibility - take ownership over how you get your work done. We're open to different working patterns and approaches. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Applications from job seekers who require sponsorship to work in the UK are welcome and will be considered alongside all other applications. Whilst this role is currently eligible for sponsorship under the Skilled Worker Route, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2573": {
      "title": "Research Assistants in Biophilic Design and Sleep Quality",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Research Assistants in Biophilic Design and Sleep Quality Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Research Assistants in Biophilic Design and Sleep Quality Apply for job Job reference: 552539 Location: City Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Construction Management Closing date: 05/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Architecture, Design and the Built Environment Salary / Grade Grade E (£28,063 - £30,185 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Research Assistants in Biophilic Design and Sleep Quality Grade E (£28,063 - £30,185 p.a. pro rata) Part time (0.3FTE) / Fixed term contract: 10 months 3 posts available About the Role We are looking for three Research Assistants to support exciting research in biophilic design and sleep quality. To undertake research activities, including questionnaire development, survey administration, data collection and analysis, and the application of quantitative research methods to support project objectives and outputs. Key Responsibilities Support research activities focused on biophilic built environments, psychology and user experience evaluation. Design, administer and analyse questionnaires and surveys to collect user feedback and behavioural data. Undertake data collection, processing and analysis using statistical and machine learning tools. Contribute to literature reviews, fieldwork and other research activities in line with project objectives. Maintain accurate research records, datasets and documentation, ensuring data quality and integrity. Support the administration and organisation of research projects, including communication with internal and external stakeholders. Share relevant findings and information with the research team and contribute to project meetings. Keep knowledge and skills up to date through continuous professional development. This role offers an opportunity to contribute to innovative research exploring how biophilic design influences occupant wellbeing and experience within the built environment. About You You will have a degree (or equivalent experience) in a relevant discipline such as Building Design, Psychology, or a related field, together with an understanding of research methods and techniques within building design and virtual reality modelling. You will be confident using specialist software and research tools, with experience of data collection, analysis and interpretation. Experience working with platforms such as Revit, Unity, or EEG data collection systems would be advantageous, alongside strong bibliographic research skills and the ability to utilise electronic library resources effectively. The successful candidate will be able to gather, organise and manage research information from a range of sources, maintain accurate records, and support research projects to agreed objectives and deadlines. You will have good problem-solving skills, including the ability to resolve routine issues independently and escalate more complex challenges when required. Strong organisational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work collaboratively as part of a research team are essential. Interviews w/c 9th November 2026 About Us We are the School of Architecture, Design and the Built Environment (ADBE) at Nottingham Trent University. We make, create, design and build. We’re planners and problem solvers. We draw lines, and we break boundaries. We are 3,000 students, five departments and one school. In the School of Architecture, Design and the Built Environment, we stand half way between science and philosophy; and between tradition and disruption. We embrace theoretical rigour and insist on providing hands-on experience for all our students. We celebrate design heritage, and we invite innovation. We’re a nationally renowned stage for talent in making and design. We investigate the physicality of tools and tech, glass and grass, and bricks and mortar. We also explore the abstract excitement of ideas and creative philosophies. For any informal queries about the role or the ADBE team, please contact Associate Professor Yangang Xing, at yangang.xing@ntu.ac.uk. Join Us 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Hybrid working - we encourage and offer a mixture of office working and working from home. You're empowered to define how you work best for the benefits of your stakeholders. Flexibility - take ownership over how you get your work done. We're open to different working patterns and approaches. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt JD/PS (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2657": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Ecosystem Acoustics",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Research Fellow in Ecosystem Acoustics Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Research Fellow in Ecosystem Acoustics Apply for job Job reference: 552622 Location: Brackenhurst Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Animal and Environmental Sciences Closing date: 17/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Animal Rural and Environmental Sciences Salary / Grade See special conditions Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Post 1- Research Fellow- Ecosystem Acoustics Salary- £33,739 - £ 38,825 per annum Full time/ Fixed term for 18 months Post 2- Research Associate- Ecosystem Acoustics Salary- £29,352 - £33,739 per annum Full time/ Fixed term for 18 months About the Role's Listening to Nature: Monitoring Biodiversity Through Sound Join an exciting government funded research project developing next-generation biodiversity monitoring technologies Nottingham Trent University is seeking two enthusiastic researchers to join the newly funded Eco-SEv project, which aims to optimise autonomous acoustic technologies for assessing biodiversity and ecosystem health across agricultural, forestry and natural environments. Working in collaboration with an innovative technology company and a consortium of industry and international partners, you will contribute to the development and validation of next-generation ecoacoustic tools for assessing biodiversity and ecosystem health across diverse environments in the UK and internationally. By combining autonomous acoustic sensors, ecological expertise and advanced analytical approaches, Eco-SEv aims to deliver scalable solutions that support environmental monitoring, natural capital assessment and sustainability across a range of agricultural, forestry and conservation settings. Available positions: Research Fellow You will lead NTU's research contribution to the project, designing and delivering acoustic monitoring studies, analysing ecological and acoustic datasets, reporting outputs and coordinating validation activities undertaken by partners in the UK and Kenya. You will work closely with leading researchers in ecoacoustics, ecology and biodiversity assessment, alongside commercial partners developing cutting-edge environmental sensing technologies. Research Associate You will support field and analytical aspects of the project, including deployment of acoustic monitoring equipment, ecological surveys, biodiversity ground-truthing, data processing and stakeholder engagement activities. This role offers an excellent opportunity for an early-career researcher wishing to develop expertise in ecoacoustics, biodiversity monitoring and environmental data science. What we are looking for We welcome applicants from disciplines such as: Ecology Conservation Biology Environmental Science Geography Bioacoustics Ecoacoustics Zoology Natural Resources Management Related environmental disciplines Candidates should ideally have experience in ecological field research and biodiversity monitoring, together with skills in data analysis, statistical modelling, GIS, and programming in R and/or Python. Familiarity with ecoacoustic methods, including the processing and analysis of acoustic datasets, use of ecoacoustic software and platforms, and management of large biodiversity databases, would be highly desirable. Experience with environmental sensors, remote sensing technologies and machine learning approaches would also be advantageous. Interview Date: w/c 30th November 2026 About Us We are the School of Animal, Rural and Environmental Science (ARES) at Nottingham Trent University. Our business is nature: specifically, the environment, animal health and welfare, ecology and conservation, and agriculture and food production.. Our approach is innovative and inclusive. We feel it makes us that little bit different. It’s our goal to have a positive impact on the planet by improving the well being of environments, animals, plants, and people. If you see that passion in yourself, we can be a new, powerful partner in your career. For any informal queries about the role or the ARES team, please contact Andy Gill , Associate Dean for Research at andy.gill@ntu.ac.uk and Antonio Uzal Fernandez, Associate Professor at antonio.uzal@ntu.ac.uk Join Us 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Hybrid working - we encourage and offer a mixture of office working and working from home. You're empowered to define how you work best for the benefits of your stakeholders. Flexibility - take ownership over how you get your work done. We're open to different working patterns and approaches. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, these roles has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2631": {
      "title": "Placement Allocation Administrator",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Placement Allocation Administrator Cookie Policy By clicking \"Allow Cookies\", you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to analyse site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Cookie Policy (Opens in a new tab) Decline Allow cookies Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Placement Allocation Administrator Apply for job Job reference: 552596 Location: Clifton Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care Closing date: 10/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Social Sciences Salary / Grade Grade E (£28,063 - £30,185 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Inspire, drive change and save lives. Doing things differently. Placement Allocation Administrator Salary- £28,063 - £30,185 per annum Full time/ Permanent About the Role We are seeking an organised and proactive Placement Allocation Administrator to join our Practice Learning team and support the delivery of high-quality placement experiences for students across Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Paramedicine, and Social Work programmes. This is a pivotal role within Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care, responsible for coordinating the allocation and administration of professional practice placements, ensuring students are placed appropriately and in line with professional, regulatory, and programme requirements. The successful candidate will be highly organised, with the ability to manage multiple priorities. You will be confident working with databases with a good attention to detail. Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills are essential, as the role requires effective collaboration with students, academic colleagues, NHS and social care partners, to support the delivery of high-quality placement experiences. Working closely with academic teams, healthcare and social care placement providers, and students, you will contribute to the smooth running of placement activity, supporting student success and maintaining positive relationships with our external partners. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to the education of future healthcare and social care professionals. You will join a supportive team committed to delivering an excellent student experience and maintaining strong partnerships with placement providers across the region. We consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. Interview Date: w/c 23rd November 2026 About Us Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care brings together expert and enthusiastic staff from across the health, social care, and social work sectors, many of whom are experienced practitioners and recognised leaders in their fields. Our academics are actively engaged in research and scholarship, with work that is widely published and directly informs our curriculum, ensuring students benefit from a contemporary, evidence-based and professionally relevant learning experience. We are committed to providing a vibrant, inclusive and supportive learning environment where teaching is grounded in research, professional practice and a strong commitment to student success. By fostering collaboration between students, practitioners, researchers and external partners, we prepare graduates to make a meaningful impact within their professions and communities. The Institute is dedicated to developing innovative education and research that addresses the challenges facing health and social care services today. Through our strong partnerships with healthcare, social care and community organisations, we strive to make a positive contribution to improving health, wellbeing and social outcomes for all. Our ambition is to equip the next generation of professionals with the knowledge, skills and values needed to lead change and improve lives in an evolving health and social care landscape. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Anne Felton Academic Director Nottingham Institute of Health and Social Care at Anne.Felton@ntu.ac.uk or Amy Underwood , Placement and Engagement Manager Amy.Underwood@ntu.ac.uk Join Us Hybrid working - We support flexible ways of working through a combination of campus-based and home working where applicable. For full-time roles, this includes a minimum of 60% on-campus commitment. We trust colleagues to work with their teams to shape working patterns that enable them to deliver the best possible outcomes for their stakeholders. Flexibility - We welcome and support a range of working patterns and approaches, helping colleagues balance their work and personal commitments while meeting the needs of the role. 28 - 30 days annual leave, plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. We are committed to advancing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion across all areas of our work. We actively promote a culture of respect and belonging and we welcome applications from people of all backgrounds. For more information please click here - Equality, Diversity and Inclusion | Nottingham Trent University And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Supporting Documents save_alt JDPS- Placement Allocation Administator (PDF, KB) Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2659": {
      "title": "Research Fellow",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Research Fellow - Agri-Tech Development Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Research Fellow - Agri-Tech Development Apply for job Job reference: 552624 Location: Brackenhurst Campus Employment type: Fixed Term Contract Team: Animal and Environmental Sciences Closing date: 02/11/2026 School / Directorate: School of Animal Rural and Environmental Sciences Salary / Grade Grade G (£33,739 - £38,825 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Build a Rewarding Career. Doing things differently. Research Fellow Agri-Tech Development Salary- £33,739 - £38,825 per annum Full time/ Fixed term for 12 months About the Role Nottingham Trent University is developing an exciting and rapidly growing portfolio of applied research in sustainable agriculture, crop production and agri-technology. Following a series of successful external funding awards and continued investment in our research infrastructure, we are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow to join our team. The successful candidate will contribute to the delivery of innovative research projects focused on controlled environment agriculture, crop production systems and agricultural innovation. Working alongside academic researchers and industry collaborators, you will support the design and implementation of experiments, collection and analysis of data, and dissemination of research findings. The role will involve work with a range of commercially relevant crops, including ornamental and agricultural species, within newly developed controlled environment facilities and other research environments. This is an excellent opportunity to contribute to impactful, industry-facing research while helping address some of the key challenges facing modern agriculture, including productivity, sustainability and resilience. About You You will have: A PhD (or be close to completion) in plant science, crop science, horticulture, agricultural science, environmental science or a related discipline. We will also consider individuals with other relevant experience. Experience of designing and conducting experimental research. Strong analytical and data management skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. The ability to work effectively both independently and within multidisciplinary teams. Experience in one or more of the following areas would be advantageous: Controlled environment agriculture. Glasshouse or protected crop production. Plant physiology. Horticultural science. Crop husbandry and production systems. Industry-facing or applied research projects. Interview Date: w/c 9th November 2026 About Us We are the School of Animal, Rural and Environmental Science (ARES) at Nottingham Trent University. Our business is nature: specifically, the environment, animal health and welfare, ecology and conservation, and agriculture and food production.. Our approach is innovative and inclusive. We feel it makes us that little bit different. It’s our goal to have a positive impact on the planet by improving the well being of environments, animals, plants, and people. If you see that passion in yourself, we can be a new, powerful partner in your career. You will become part of a dynamic and collaborative research environment within NTU's School of Animal, Rural and Environmental Sciences, supporting projects that are delivering real-world impact through close partnership with industry. Our team has recently secured significant investment through competitive funding programmes and is expanding its research facilities and capability in controlled environment agriculture and sustainable crop production. This post offers an exciting opportunity to help shape this growing area of research while developing your own academic and professional profile For any informal queries about the role or the ARES team, please contact Andy Gill (Associate Dean for Research) at andy.gill@ntu.ac.uk Join Us 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Hybrid working - we encourage and offer a mixture of office working and working from home. You're empowered to define how you work best for the benefits of your stakeholders. Flexibility - take ownership over how you get your work done. We're open to different working patterns and approaches. Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Access to a wealth of formal and informal professional development opportunities to develop your skills and advance your career. Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe and Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Please note that unfortunately, this role has been assessed as ineligible for sponsorship under the UK Visas & Immigration points-based immigration system however, we recommend that you assess your eligibility before applying for this position. For more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. However, applications are welcome from candidates who do not currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a valid visa via another route. Please consult the Home Office website for further information. Please note that this role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2605": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Operations and Supply Chain Management",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Operations and Supply Chain Management Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Operations and Supply Chain Management Apply for job Job reference: 552570 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Strategy, Analytics and Operations Closing date: 08/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Business School Salary / Grade HE Lecturer or Senior Lecturer (£39,984 - £58,624 pa pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Empower Future Leaders. Doing things differently. Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Operations and Supply Chain Management Lecturer £39,984 – £44,977 Senior Lecturer £46,320 - £58,624 About the Role The Department of Strategy, Analytics and Operations at Nottingham Business School is actively looking for an enthusiastic and motivated individual to join us as Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Operations and Supply Chain Management. We are seeking a candidate who can contribute to the delivery of our existing experiential learning and teaching success of various supply chain management modules in our UG & PG programmes. The ideal candidate should have a strong record of professional practice in supply chain management and scholarship activities. This role is diverse, providing opportunities to contribute to a wide range of teaching and teaching-related activities across all levels. Responsibilities include engaging in module management and development tasks, as well as working closely with colleagues across the department to support the school's personalisation strategy. Additionally, the role offers the chance for individuals to utilise their knowledge in designing academic content for students. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. Interview Date: w/c 23rd November 2026 About Us Nottingham Business School (NBS) delivers research and education that combine academic excellence with real-world impact on people, business, and society. We lead in experiential learning and personalised education, and our research drives positive change across social and economic spheres. This informs all our programmes, from undergraduate to doctoral. With strong partnerships across business, public, and voluntary sectors, NBS is known as the business school for business. We hold the prestigious Triple Crown Accreditation (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA), placing us in the top 1% of business schools worldwide. Discover more on our website . At NTU, we do things differently. Join one of Europe’s largest and most innovative business schools to help shape inclusive research and make a real difference. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact either Demola Obembe – Head of Department ( demola.obembe@ntu.ac.uk ) or Michael Hewitt – Assistant Head of Department ( michael.hewitt@ntu.ac.uk ). Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe & Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
    },
    "https://vacancies.ntu.ac.uk/Job/JobDetail?JobId=2606": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer Business Analytics and Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "NTU | Jobs | Search here for your perfect career - Job Information  | Apply for Senior Lecturer Business Analytics and Artificial Intelligence Skip to main content List Vacancies (current) Sign in Accessibility Tools List Vacancies (current) Back to Search Results Senior Lecturer Business Analytics and Artificial Intelligence Apply for job Job reference: 552571 Location: City Campus Employment type: Permanent Contract Team: Strategy, Analytics and Operations Closing date: 08/11/2026 School / Directorate: Nottingham Business School Salary / Grade HE Senior Lecturer (£46,320 - £58,624 p.a. pro rata) Where to find us location_on Get directions Empower Future Leaders. Doing things differently. Senior Lecturer in Business Analytics and Artificial Intelligence Salary £46,320- £58,624 Full time About the Role The Department of Strategy, Analytics and Operations at Nottingham Business School is actively looking for an enthusiastic and motivated individual to join us as Senior Lecturer in Business Analytics and Artificial Intelligence. We are seeking a candidate who can contribute to the delivery of our existing experiential learning and teaching success of various supply chain management modules in our UG & PG programmes. The ideal candidate should have a strong record of professional practice in the subject area and scholarship activities. This role is diverse, providing opportunities to contribute to a wide range of teaching and teaching-related activities across all levels. Responsibilities include engaging in module management and development tasks, as well as working closely with colleagues across the department to support the school's personalisation strategy. Additionally, the role offers the chance for individuals to utilise their knowledge in designing academic content for students. For more details, please take a look at the role profile. We'll still consider applications even if you don't meet every single one of the requirements, so don't be put off if you don't match them perfectly. To ensure the diverse needs of our team are met we actively encourage secondments and offer flexible part-time working patterns - we're focused on finding the right person for the role. Interview Date: w/c 23rd November 2026 About Us Nottingham Business School (NBS) delivers research and education that combine academic excellence with real-world impact on people, business, and society. We lead in experiential learning and personalised education, and our research drives positive change across social and economic spheres. This informs all our programmes, from undergraduate to doctoral. With strong partnerships across business, public, and voluntary sectors, NBS is known as the business school for business. We hold the prestigious Triple Crown Accreditation (EQUIS, AACSB, AMBA), placing us in the top 1% of business schools worldwide. Discover more on our website . At NTU, we do things differently. Join one of Europe’s largest and most innovative business schools to help shape inclusive research and make a real difference. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact either Demola Obembe – Head of Department ( demola.obembe@ntu.ac.uk ) or Michael Hewitt – Assistant Head of Department ( michael.hewitt@ntu.ac.uk ). Join Us Find out more about our academic community at NTU, including the support we offer to academics at all stages of their careers. We also offer: 30 - 35 days annual leave per year plus statutory bank holidays and 5 university closure days pro rata Salary Sacrifice Retirement Savings Plan with life assurance and income protection. Available to colleagues who choose to opt out of the contractual pension scheme. Minimum colleague contributions of 0% matched with minimum NTU contributions of 8%. Opportunity to receive a bonus for exceptional performance and contribution Range of health and wellbeing services, including a Health Cash Plan, voluntary benefits, discounts, and savings for all colleagues. And a whole lot more…Find out more about the range of benefits we offer. Come and be part of our success. Apply today. Safe & Inclusive At NTU, we continue to build an inclusive culture that encourages, supports and celebrates the diverse voices and experiences of our students and colleagues. By championing positive wellbeing, we promote an environment where all can thrive and reach their full potential. We welcome the unique contributions that you can bring and we encourage people from underrepresented communities and backgrounds to apply to join our team. Depending on your individual circumstances this role may be eligible for sponsorship under the UKVI Skilled Worker route. We recommend that you review your individual circumstances before applying, or for more information visit the Government Skilled Worker visa support page. This role is covered by the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act (1974) and successful applicants will be asked to declare any unspent criminal convictions. Take a look around the company https://www.ntu.ac.uk/ Apply for job favorite_border Save this job Go to main site Terms & Conditions Accessibility Nottingham Trent University applicant tracking system delivered and supported by Jobtrain"
